    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Act to apply to courts in respect of administrative matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "Courts other than courts of Norfolk Island—general\n(1) For the purposes of this Act:\n(a) a court (other than a court of Norfolk Island) shall be deemed\nto be a prescribed authority;\n(b) the holder of a judicial office (other than a judicial office in a\ncourt of Norfolk Island) or other office pertaining to a court\n(other than a court of Norfolk Island) in his or her capacity as\nthe holder of that office, being an office established by the\nlegislation establishing the court, shall be deemed not to be a\nprescribed authority and shall not be included in a\nDepartment; and",
      "skos:definition": "Courts other than courts of Norfolk Island—general\n(1) For the purposes of this Act:\n(a) a court (other than a court of Norfolk Island) shall be deemed\nto be a prescribed authority;\n(b) the holder of a judicial office (other than a judicial office in a\ncourt of Norfolk Island) or other office pertaining to a court\n(other than a court of Norfolk Island) in his or her capacity as\nthe holder of that office, being an office established by the\nlegislation establishing the court, shall be deemed not to be a\nprescribed authority and shall not be included in a\nDepartment; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "396b9f9fd667cc9e41c706602ba4e04d0c8113f74a665515c1ed017f342b6c98",
      "skos:note": "A court other than a court of Norfolk Island shall be deemed a prescribed authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Act to apply to courts in respect of administrative matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "Courts other than courts of Norfolk Island—general\n(1) For the purposes of this Act:\n(a) a court (other than a court of Norfolk Island) shall be deemed\nto be a prescribed authority;\n(b) the holder of a judicial office (other than a judicial office in a\ncourt of Norfolk Island) or other office pertaining to a court\n(other than a court of Norfolk Island) in his or her capacity as\nthe holder of that office, being an office established by the\nlegislation establishing the court, shall be deemed not to be a\nprescribed authority and shall not be included in a\nDepartment; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "DEEMED",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implies obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Act to apply to certain tribunals in respect of administrative",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "matters\nFor the purposes of this Act:\n(a) each tribunal, authority or body specified in Schedule 1 is\ndeemed to be a prescribed authority;\n(b) the holder of an office pertaining to a tribunal, authority or\nbody specified in Schedule 1, being an office established by\nthe legislation establishing the tribunal, authority or body so\nspecified in his or her capacity as the holder of that office, is\nnot to be taken to be a prescribed authority or to be included\nin a Department; and\n(c) a registry or other office of or under the charge of a tribunal,\nauthority or body specified in Schedule 1, and the staff of\nsuch a registry or other office when acting in a capacity as\nmembers of that staff, shall be taken as a part of the tribunal,\nauthority or body so specified as a prescribed authority;\nbut this Act does not apply to any request for access to a document\nof a tribunal, authority or body so specified unless the document\nrelates to matters of an administrative nature.",
      "skos:definition": "matters\nFor the purposes of this Act:\n(a) each tribunal, authority or body specified in Schedule 1 is\ndeemed to be a prescribed authority;\n(b) the holder of an office pertaining to a tribunal, authority or\nbody specified in Schedule 1, being an office established by\nthe legislation establishing the tribunal, authority or body so\nspecified in his or her capacity as the holder of that office, is\nnot to be taken to be a prescribed authority or to be included\nin a Department; and\n(c) a registry or other office of or under the charge of a tribunal,\nauthority or body specified in Schedule 1, and the staff of\nsuch a registry or other office when acting in a capacity as\nmembers of that staff, shall be taken as a part of the tribunal,\nauthority or body so specified as a prescribed authority;\nbut this Act does not apply to any request for access to a document\nof a tribunal, authority or body so specified unless the document\nrelates to matters of an administrative nature.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-6-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-6-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "508ffc56b8b2fd854d22b6d15c2d3bb29c4dedbbf7784accc4bfe964fc60a878",
      "skos:note": "Tribunals, authorities, and bodies specified in Schedule 1 are deemed prescribed authorities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Act to apply to certain tribunals in respect of administrative",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "matters\nFor the purposes of this Act:\n(a) each tribunal, authority or body specified in Schedule 1 is\ndeemed to be a prescribed authority;\n(b) the holder of an office pertaining to a tribunal, authority or\nbody specified in Schedule 1, being an office established by\nthe legislation establishing the tribunal, authority or body so\nspecified in his or her capacity as the holder of that office, is\nnot to be taken to be a prescribed authority or to be included\nin a Department; and\n(c) a registry or other office of or under the charge of a tribunal,\nauthority or body specified in Schedule 1, and the staff of\nsuch a registry or other office when acting in a capacity as\nmembers of that staff, shall be taken as a part of the tribunal,\nauthority or body so specified as a prescribed authority;\nbut this Act does not apply to any request for access to a document\nof a tribunal, authority or body so specified unless the document\nrelates to matters of an administrative nature."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-6-norm",
