    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8A Information to be published—what is operational information?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-8a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency’s operational information is information held by the\nagency to assist the agency to perform or exercise the agency’s\nfunctions or powers in making decisions or recommendations\naffecting members of the public (or any particular person or entity,\nor class of persons or entities).\nExample:\nThe agency’s rules, guidelines, practices and precedents relating to\nthose decisions and recommendations.\n(2) An agency’s operational information does not include information\nthat is available to members of the public otherwise than by being\npublished by (or on behalf of) the agency.\n8B  Information to be published—accuracy etc.\nAn agency must ensure that information published by the agency\nas required or permitted by this Part is accurate, up-to-date and\ncomplete.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An agency’s operational information is information held by the\nagency to assist the agency to perform or exercise the agency’s\nfunctions or powers in making decisions or recommendations\naffecting members of the public (or any particular person or entity,\nor class of persons or entities).\nExample:\nThe agency’s rules, guidelines, practices and precedents relating to\nthose decisions and recommendations.\n(2) An agency’s operational information does not include information\nthat is available to members of the public otherwise than by being\npublished by (or on behalf of) the agency.\n8B  Information to be published—accuracy etc.\nAn agency must ensure that information published by the agency\nas required or permitted by this Part is accurate, up-to-date and\ncomplete.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3121c8c9f5b772aec58d09a698ba94ff9659ddf942fd17f3b322ab3d8fc1d282"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-8a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8A Information to be published—what is operational information?",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency’s operational information is information held by the\nagency to assist the agency to perform or exercise the agency’s\nfunctions or powers in making decisions or recommendations\naffecting members of the public (or any particular person or entity,\nor class of persons or entities).\nExample:\nThe agency’s rules, guidelines, practices and precedents relating to\nthose decisions and recommendations.\n(2) An agency’s operational information does not include information\nthat is available to members of the public otherwise than by being\npublished by (or on behalf of) the agency.\n8B  Information to be published—accuracy etc.\nAn agency must ensure that information published by the agency\nas required or permitted by this Part is accurate, up-to-date and\ncomplete."
    },
