    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8d-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8D(4) Information to be published—how (and to whom) information is",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-8d-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The agency may impose a charge on a person for accessing the\ninformation only if:\n(a) the person does not directly access the information by\ndownloading it from the website (or another website); and\n(b) the charge is to reimburse the agency for specific\nreproduction costs, or other specific incidental costs, incurred\nin giving the person access to that particular information.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The agency may impose a charge on a person for accessing the\ninformation only if:\n(a) the person does not directly access the information by\ndownloading it from the website (or another website); and\n(b) the charge is to reimburse the agency for specific\nreproduction costs, or other specific incidental costs, incurred\nin giving the person access to that particular information.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8d-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-8d-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a3a14a2d4dddec0c28797b59cf20fbd4d3a9c74ac1a21d7e7f64371ffa548be",
      "skos:note": "Agency may impose charge for accessing information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-8d-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8D(4) Information to be published—how (and to whom) information is",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The agency may impose a charge on a person for accessing the\ninformation only if:\n(a) the person does not directly access the information by\ndownloading it from the website (or another website); and\n(b) the charge is to reimburse the agency for specific\nreproduction costs, or other specific incidental costs, incurred\nin giving the person access to that particular information."
    },
