    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Unpublished operational information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) part (or all) of an agency’s operational information (the\nunpublished information), in relation to a function or power\nof the agency, is not published by the agency in accordance\nwith this Part; and\n(b) a person engages in conduct relevant to the performance of\nthe function or the exercise of the power; and\n(c) at the time of engaging in that conduct:\n(i) the person was not aware of the unpublished\ninformation; and\n(ii) the agency had been in existence for more than 12\nmonths.\nNote:\nAn agency’s operational information is required to be published by the\nagency (see sections 8 and 8A).\nNo prejudice from lack of awareness of unpublished information\n(2) The person must not be subjected to any prejudice only because of\nthe application to that conduct of any rule, guideline or practice in\nthe unpublished information, if the person could lawfully have\navoided that prejudice had he or she been aware of the unpublished\ninformation.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) part (or all) of an agency’s operational information (the\nunpublished information), in relation to a function or power\nof the agency, is not published by the agency in accordance\nwith this Part; and\n(b) a person engages in conduct relevant to the performance of\nthe function or the exercise of the power; and\n(c) at the time of engaging in that conduct:\n(i) the person was not aware of the unpublished\ninformation; and\n(ii) the agency had been in existence for more than 12\nmonths.\nNote:\nAn agency’s operational information is required to be published by the\nagency (see sections 8 and 8A).\nNo prejudice from lack of awareness of unpublished information\n(2) The person must not be subjected to any prejudice only because of\nthe application to that conduct of any rule, guideline or practice in\nthe unpublished information, if the person could lawfully have\navoided that prejudice had he or she been aware of the unpublished\ninformation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-10-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-10-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Unpublished operational information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) part (or all) of an agency’s operational information (the\nunpublished information), in relation to a function or power\nof the agency, is not published by the agency in accordance\nwith this Part; and\n(b) a person engages in conduct relevant to the performance of\nthe function or the exercise of the power; and\n(c) at the time of engaging in that conduct:\n(i) the person was not aware of the unpublished\ninformation; and\n(ii) the agency had been in existence for more than 12\nmonths.\nNote:\nAn agency’s operational information is required to be published by the\nagency (see sections 8 and 8A).\nNo prejudice from lack of awareness of unpublished information\n(2) The person must not be subjected to any prejudice only because of\nthe application to that conduct of any rule, guideline or practice in\nthe unpublished information, if the person could lawfully have\navoided that prejudice had he or she been aware of the unpublished\ninformation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-10-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10(1) Unpublished operational information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
