    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-11c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11C(4) Publication of information in accessed documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-11c-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The agency may impose a charge on a person for accessing the\ninformation only if:\n(a) the person does not directly access the information by\ndownloading it from the website (or another website); and\n(b) the charge is to reimburse the agency for a specific\nreproduction cost, or other specific incidental costs, incurred\nin giving the person access to that particular information.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The agency may impose a charge on a person for accessing the\ninformation only if:\n(a) the person does not directly access the information by\ndownloading it from the website (or another website); and\n(b) the charge is to reimburse the agency for a specific\nreproduction cost, or other specific incidental costs, incurred\nin giving the person access to that particular information.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-11c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-11c-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-11c-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "40b2a1799a3a83f16f3364655bc10c1ae8341063469b3811c1eadedb878eb35b",
      "skos:note": "Agency may impose charge for accessing information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-11c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11C(4) Publication of information in accessed documents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The agency may impose a charge on a person for accessing the\ninformation only if:\n(a) the person does not directly access the information by\ndownloading it from the website (or another website); and\n(b) the charge is to reimburse the agency for a specific\nreproduction cost, or other specific incidental costs, incurred\nin giving the person access to that particular information."
    },
