      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subject to subsection 17(1), where a person requests access to a\ndocument in a particular form and, for a reason specified in\nsubsection (3), access in that form is refused but access is given in\nanother form, the applicant shall not be required to pay a charge in\nrespect of the provision of access to the document that is greater\nthan the charge that he or she would have been required to pay if\naccess had been given in the form requested.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Subject to subsection 17(1), where a person requests access to a\ndocument in a particular form and, for a reason specified in\nsubsection (3), access in that form is refused but access is given in\nanother form, the applicant shall not be required to pay a charge in\nrespect of the provision of access to the document that is greater\nthan the charge that he or she would have been required to pay if\naccess had been given in the form requested.",
      "values:partOf": {
