    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Deferment of access",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency which, or a Minister who, receives a request may defer\nthe provision of access to the document concerned:\n(a) if the publication of the document concerned is required by\nlaw—until the expiration of the period within which the\ndocument is required to be published; or\n(b) if the document concerned has been prepared for presentation\nto Parliament or for the purpose of being made available to a\nparticular person or body or with the intention that it should\nbe so made available—until the expiration of a reasonable\nperiod after its preparation for it to be so presented or made\navailable; or\n(c) if the premature release of the document concerned would be\ncontrary to the public interest—until the occurrence of any\nevent after which or the expiration of any period of time\nbeyond which the release of the document would not be\ncontrary to the public interest; or\n(d) if a Minister considers that the document concerned is of\nsuch general public interest that the Parliament should be\ninformed of the contents of the document before the\ndocument is otherwise made public—until the expiration of\n5 sitting days of either House of the Parliament.\n(2) Where the provision of access to a document is deferred in\naccordance with subsection (1), the agency or Minister shall, in\ninforming the applicant of the reasons for the decision, indicate, as\nfar as practicable, the period for which the deferment will operate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An agency which, or a Minister who, receives a request may defer\nthe provision of access to the document concerned:\n(a) if the publication of the document concerned is required by\nlaw—until the expiration of the period within which the\ndocument is required to be published; or\n(b) if the document concerned has been prepared for presentation\nto Parliament or for the purpose of being made available to a\nparticular person or body or with the intention that it should\nbe so made available—until the expiration of a reasonable\nperiod after its preparation for it to be so presented or made\navailable; or\n(c) if the premature release of the document concerned would be\ncontrary to the public interest—until the occurrence of any\nevent after which or the expiration of any period of time\nbeyond which the release of the document would not be\ncontrary to the public interest; or\n(d) if a Minister considers that the document concerned is of\nsuch general public interest that the Parliament should be\ninformed of the contents of the document before the\ndocument is otherwise made public—until the expiration of\n5 sitting days of either House of the Parliament.\n(2) Where the provision of access to a document is deferred in\naccordance with subsection (1), the agency or Minister shall, in\ninforming the applicant of the reasons for the decision, indicate, as\nfar as practicable, the period for which the deferment will operate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-21-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d810c7280b546f6f1a4108e71332ab92d1abbc0612fae4b7bc87abdc913cad12"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Deferment of access",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency which, or a Minister who, receives a request may defer\nthe provision of access to the document concerned:\n(a) if the publication of the document concerned is required by\nlaw—until the expiration of the period within which the\ndocument is required to be published; or\n(b) if the document concerned has been prepared for presentation\nto Parliament or for the purpose of being made available to a\nparticular person or body or with the intention that it should\nbe so made available—until the expiration of a reasonable\nperiod after its preparation for it to be so presented or made\navailable; or\n(c) if the premature release of the document concerned would be\ncontrary to the public interest—until the occurrence of any\nevent after which or the expiration of any period of time\nbeyond which the release of the document would not be\ncontrary to the public interest; or\n(d) if a Minister considers that the document concerned is of\nsuch general public interest that the Parliament should be\ninformed of the contents of the document before the\ndocument is otherwise made public—until the expiration of\n5 sitting days of either House of the Parliament.\n(2) Where the provision of access to a document is deferred in\naccordance with subsection (1), the agency or Minister shall, in\ninforming the applicant of the reasons for the decision, indicate, as\nfar as practicable, the period for which the deferment will operate."
    },
