    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22 Access to edited copies with exempt or irrelevant matter deleted",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister decides:\n(i) to refuse to give access to an exempt document; or\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 22\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(ii) that to give access to a document would disclose\ninformation that would reasonably be regarded as\nirrelevant to the request for access; and\n(b) it is possible for the agency or Minister to prepare a copy (an\nedited copy) of the document, modified by deletions,\nensuring that:\n(i) access to the edited copy would be required to be given\nunder section 11A (access to documents on request);\nand\n(ii) the edited copy would not disclose any information that\nwould reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the\nrequest; and\n(c) it is reasonably practicable for the agency or Minister to\nprepare the edited copy, having regard to:\n(i) the nature and extent of the modification; and\n(ii) the resources available to modify the document; and\n(d) it is not apparent (from the request or from consultation with\nthe applicant) that the applicant would decline access to the\nedited copy.\nAccess to edited copy\n(2) The agency or Minister must:\n(a) prepare the edited copy as mentioned in paragraph (1)(b); and\n(b) give the applicant access to the edited copy.\nNotice to applicant\n(3) The agency or Minister must give the applicant notice in writing:\n(a) that the edited copy has been prepared; and\n(b) of the grounds for the deletions; and\n(c) if any matter deleted is exempt matter—that the matter\ndeleted is exempt matter because of a specified provision of\nthis Act.\n(4) Section 26 (reasons for decision) does not apply to the decision to\nrefuse access to the whole document unless the applicant requests",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister decides:\n(i) to refuse to give access to an exempt document; or\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 22\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(ii) that to give access to a document would disclose\ninformation that would reasonably be regarded as\nirrelevant to the request for access; and\n(b) it is possible for the agency or Minister to prepare a copy (an\nedited copy) of the document, modified by deletions,\nensuring that:\n(i) access to the edited copy would be required to be given\nunder section 11A (access to documents on request);\nand\n(ii) the edited copy would not disclose any information that\nwould reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the\nrequest; and\n(c) it is reasonably practicable for the agency or Minister to\nprepare the edited copy, having regard to:\n(i) the nature and extent of the modification; and\n(ii) the resources available to modify the document; and\n(d) it is not apparent (from the request or from consultation with\nthe applicant) that the applicant would decline access to the\nedited copy.\nAccess to edited copy\n(2) The agency or Minister must:\n(a) prepare the edited copy as mentioned in paragraph (1)(b); and\n(b) give the applicant access to the edited copy.\nNotice to applicant\n(3) The agency or Minister must give the applicant notice in writing:\n(a) that the edited copy has been prepared; and\n(b) of the grounds for the deletions; and\n(c) if any matter deleted is exempt matter—that the matter\ndeleted is exempt matter because of a specified provision of\nthis Act.\n(4) Section 26 (reasons for decision) does not apply to the decision to\nrefuse access to the whole document unless the applicant requests",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-22-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-22-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-22-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-22-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22 Access to edited copies with exempt or irrelevant matter deleted",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister decides:\n(i) to refuse to give access to an exempt document; or\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 22\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(ii) that to give access to a document would disclose\ninformation that would reasonably be regarded as\nirrelevant to the request for access; and\n(b) it is possible for the agency or Minister to prepare a copy (an\nedited copy) of the document, modified by deletions,\nensuring that:\n(i) access to the edited copy would be required to be given\nunder section 11A (access to documents on request);\nand\n(ii) the edited copy would not disclose any information that\nwould reasonably be regarded as irrelevant to the\nrequest; and\n(c) it is reasonably practicable for the agency or Minister to\nprepare the edited copy, having regard to:\n(i) the nature and extent of the modification; and\n(ii) the resources available to modify the document; and\n(d) it is not apparent (from the request or from consultation with\nthe applicant) that the applicant would decline access to the\nedited copy.\nAccess to edited copy\n(2) The agency or Minister must:\n(a) prepare the edited copy as mentioned in paragraph (1)(b); and\n(b) give the applicant access to the edited copy.\nNotice to applicant\n(3) The agency or Minister must give the applicant notice in writing:\n(a) that the edited copy has been prepared; and\n(b) of the grounds for the deletions; and\n(c) if any matter deleted is exempt matter—that the matter\ndeleted is exempt matter because of a specified provision of\nthis Act.\n(4) Section 26 (reasons for decision) does not apply to the decision to\nrefuse access to the whole document unless the applicant requests"
    },
