    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23(2) Decisions to be made by authorised persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-23-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A decision in respect of a request made to a court, or made to a\ntribunal, authority or body that is specified in Schedule 1, may be\nmade on behalf of that court, tribunal, authority or body by the\nprincipal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body or,\nsubject to the regulations, by an officer of that court, tribunal,\nauthority or body acting within the scope of authority exercisable\nby him or her in accordance with arrangements approved by the\nprincipal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body.\n24  Power to refuse request—diversion of resources etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A decision in respect of a request made to a court, or made to a\ntribunal, authority or body that is specified in Schedule 1, may be\nmade on behalf of that court, tribunal, authority or body by the\nprincipal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body or,\nsubject to the regulations, by an officer of that court, tribunal,\nauthority or body acting within the scope of authority exercisable\nby him or her in accordance with arrangements approved by the\nprincipal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body.\n24  Power to refuse request—diversion of resources etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
