    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23(2) Decisions to be made by authorised persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-23-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (3), but without limiting the matters to which\nthe agency or Minister may have regard, in deciding whether a\npractical refusal reason exists, the agency or Minister must have\nregard to the resources that would have to be used for the\nfollowing:\n(a) identifying, locating or collating the documents within the\nfiling system of the agency, or the office of the Minister;\n(b) deciding whether to grant, refuse or defer access to a\ndocument to which the request relates, or to grant access to\nan edited copy of such a document, including resources that\nwould have to be used for:\n(i) examining the document; or\n(ii) consulting with any person or body in relation to the\nrequest;\n(c) making a copy, or an edited copy, of the document;\n(d) notifying any interim or final decision on the request.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subject to subsection (3), but without limiting the matters to which\nthe agency or Minister may have regard, in deciding whether a\npractical refusal reason exists, the agency or Minister must have\nregard to the resources that would have to be used for the\nfollowing:\n(a) identifying, locating or collating the documents within the\nfiling system of the agency, or the office of the Minister;\n(b) deciding whether to grant, refuse or defer access to a\ndocument to which the request relates, or to grant access to\nan edited copy of such a document, including resources that\nwould have to be used for:\n(i) examining the document; or\n(ii) consulting with any person or body in relation to the\nrequest;\n(c) making a copy, or an edited copy, of the document;\n(d) notifying any interim or final decision on the request.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-ltl-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-deontic-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-logic-deontic-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fa624fe4ee6f2f437b5d79ccc2b352e19bb5108d2367be0fe0d2ad1d0eddb53f",
      "skos:note": "Authorized persons can make decisions on behalf of specified courts, tribunals, authorities or bodies. Agency or Minister must consider resources for decision-making. Agency or Minister may treat multiple requests as a single request if satisfied that they relate to the same document or documents."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-23-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23(2) Decisions to be made by authorised persons",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (3), but without limiting the matters to which\nthe agency or Minister may have regard, in deciding whether a\npractical refusal reason exists, the agency or Minister must have\nregard to the resources that would have to be used for the\nfollowing:\n(a) identifying, locating or collating the documents within the\nfiling system of the agency, or the office of the Minister;\n(b) deciding whether to grant, refuse or defer access to a\ndocument to which the request relates, or to grant access to\nan edited copy of such a document, including resources that\nwould have to be used for:\n(i) examining the document; or\n(ii) consulting with any person or body in relation to the\nrequest;\n(c) making a copy, or an edited copy, of the document;\n(d) notifying any interim or final decision on the request."
    },
