    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A Requests may be refused if documents cannot be found, do not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "exist or have not been received\nDocument lost or non-existent\n(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a\ndocument if:\n(a) all reasonable steps have been taken to find the document;\nand\n(b) the agency or Minister is satisfied that the document:\n(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be\nfound; or\n(ii) does not exist.\nDocument not received as required by contract\n(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if:\n(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken\ncontractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;\nand\n(b) the agency has not received the document; and\n(c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the\ndocument in accordance with those contractual measures.",
      "skos:definition": "exist or have not been received\nDocument lost or non-existent\n(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a\ndocument if:\n(a) all reasonable steps have been taken to find the document;\nand\n(b) the agency or Minister is satisfied that the document:\n(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be\nfound; or\n(ii) does not exist.\nDocument not received as required by contract\n(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if:\n(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken\ncontractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;\nand\n(b) the agency has not received the document; and\n(c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the\ndocument in accordance with those contractual measures.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6109d5d48d5056a074b455723588bde86624a8be6f3014a0f4de8853077f8328"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-24a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A Requests may be refused if documents cannot be found, do not",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "exist or have not been received\nDocument lost or non-existent\n(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a\ndocument if:\n(a) all reasonable steps have been taken to find the document;\nand\n(b) the agency or Minister is satisfied that the document:\n(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be\nfound; or\n(ii) does not exist.\nDocument not received as required by contract\n(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if:\n(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken\ncontractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;\nand\n(b) the agency has not received the document; and\n(c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the\ndocument in accordance with those contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A(1) Requests may be refused if documents cannot be found, do not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a\ndocument if:\n(a) all reasonable steps have been taken to find the document;\nand\n(b) the agency or Minister is satisfied that the document:\n(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be\nfound; or\n(ii) does not exist.\nDocument not received as required by contract",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a\ndocument if:\n(a) all reasonable steps have been taken to find the document;\nand\n(b) the agency or Minister is satisfied that the document:\n(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be\nfound; or\n(ii) does not exist.\nDocument not received as required by contract",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1-norm"
        },
