      "skos:note": "Refusal of document access request"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A(1) Requests may be refused if documents cannot be found, do not",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a\ndocument if:\n(a) all reasonable steps have been taken to find the document;\nand\n(b) the agency or Minister is satisfied that the document:\n(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be\nfound; or\n(ii) does not exist.\nDocument not received as required by contract"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency or Minister may refuse request",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) An agency or Minister may refuse a request for access to a document..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal overlap between request and agency's possession",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) is in the agency’s or Minister’s possession but cannot be found;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24A(2) Requests may be refused if documents cannot be found, do not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if:\n(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken\ncontractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;\nand\n(b) the agency has not received the document; and\n(c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the\ndocument in accordance with those contractual measures.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if:\n(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken\ncontractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;\nand\n(b) the agency has not received the document; and\n(c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the\ndocument in accordance with those contractual measures.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ceaaecc3670df3a5d1ea3846247c0db094c15047093f0688f58a5bfeb4f1872",
      "skos:note": "Agency may refuse request if document cannot be found or received through contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24A(2) Requests may be refused if documents cannot be found, do not",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if:\n(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken\ncontractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;\nand\n(b) the agency has not received the document; and\n(c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the\ndocument in accordance with those contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency has a duty to refuse request.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the agency has not received the document;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal overlap between request and receipt.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the agency has not received the document;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...and (c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the document in accordance with those contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurring",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency's efforts to receive document are recurring.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the agency has not received the document;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...and (c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the document in accordance with those contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Propagation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Document receipt is propagated through contractual measures.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken contractual measures to ensure that it receives the document;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...and (c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the document in accordance with those contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2-logic-argumentation-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency's refusal is implied by lack of receipt.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the agency has not received the document;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...and (c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the document in accordance with those contractual measures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Information as to existence of certain documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Nothing in this Act shall be taken to require an agency or Minister\nto give information as to the existence or non-existence of a\ndocument where information as to the existence or non-existence\nof that document, if included in a document of an agency, would\ncause the last-mentioned document to be:\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 26\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).\n(2) If a request relates to a document that is, or if it existed would be,\nof a kind referred to in subsection (1), the agency or Minister\ndealing with the request may give notice in writing to the applicant\nthat the agency or the Minister (as the case may be) neither\nconfirms nor denies the existence, as a document of the agency or\nan official document of the Minister, of such a document but that,\nassuming the existence of such a document, it would be:\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).\n(3) If a notice is given under subsection (2) of this section:\n(a) section 26 applies as if the decision to give the notice were a\ndecision referred to in that section; and\n(b) the decision is taken, for the purposes of Part VI, to be a\ndecision refusing to grant access to the document in\naccordance with the request referred to in subsection (2) of\nthis section, for the reason that the document would, if it\nexisted, be:\n(i) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(ii) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Nothing in this Act shall be taken to require an agency or Minister\nto give information as to the existence or non-existence of a\ndocument where information as to the existence or non-existence\nof that document, if included in a document of an agency, would\ncause the last-mentioned document to be:\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 26\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).\n(2) If a request relates to a document that is, or if it existed would be,\nof a kind referred to in subsection (1), the agency or Minister\ndealing with the request may give notice in writing to the applicant\nthat the agency or the Minister (as the case may be) neither\nconfirms nor denies the existence, as a document of the agency or\nan official document of the Minister, of such a document but that,\nassuming the existence of such a document, it would be:\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).\n(3) If a notice is given under subsection (2) of this section:\n(a) section 26 applies as if the decision to give the notice were a\ndecision referred to in that section; and\n(b) the decision is taken, for the purposes of Part VI, to be a\ndecision refusing to grant access to the document in\naccordance with the request referred to in subsection (2) of\nthis section, for the reason that the document would, if it\nexisted, be:\n(i) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(ii) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-25-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-25-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "52123d4b459b237794f7b826f92dcab89dd13bfc7def76c875dec702ed152768"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Information as to existence of certain documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Nothing in this Act shall be taken to require an agency or Minister\nto give information as to the existence or non-existence of a\ndocument where information as to the existence or non-existence\nof that document, if included in a document of an agency, would\ncause the last-mentioned document to be:\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 26\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).\n(2) If a request relates to a document that is, or if it existed would be,\nof a kind referred to in subsection (1), the agency or Minister\ndealing with the request may give notice in writing to the applicant\nthat the agency or the Minister (as the case may be) neither\nconfirms nor denies the existence, as a document of the agency or\nan official document of the Minister, of such a document but that,\nassuming the existence of such a document, it would be:\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3).\n(3) If a notice is given under subsection (2) of this section:\n(a) section 26 applies as if the decision to give the notice were a\ndecision referred to in that section; and\n(b) the decision is taken, for the purposes of Part VI, to be a\ndecision refusing to grant access to the document in\naccordance with the request referred to in subsection (2) of\nthis section, for the reason that the document would, if it\nexisted, be:\n(i) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(ii) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-25-ss-1",
