      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1460dd948a6c5719b91c0cb875905503e4566ec0ab5d4b1dee27329babb4515d",
      "skos:note": "Agency or Minister must provide notice if a document exists but is exempt from disclosure.",
      "dc:description": "Notice in writing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-25-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25(2) Information as to existence of certain documents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a request relates to a document that is, or if it existed would be,\nof a kind referred to in subsection (1), the agency or Minister\ndealing with the request may give notice in writing to the applicant\nthat the agency or the Minister (as the case may be) neither\nconfirms nor denies the existence, as a document of the agency or\nan official document of the Minister, of such a document but that,\nassuming the existence of such a document, it would be:\n(a) an exempt document by virtue of section 33 or\nsubsection 37(1) or 45A(1); or\n(b) an exempt document to the extent referred to in\nsubsection 45A(2) or (3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-25-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
