    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-26a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26A Consultation—documents affecting Commonwealth-State",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-26a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "relations etc.\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 26A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) arrangements have been entered into between the\nCommonwealth and a State about consultation under this\nsection; and\n(b) a request is made to an agency or Minister for access to a\ndocument that:\n(i) originated with, or was received from, the State or an\nauthority of the State; or\n(ii) contains information (State-originated information)\nthat originated with, or was received from, the State or\nan authority of the State; and\n(c) it appears to the agency or Minister that the State may\nreasonably wish to contend that:\n(i) the document is conditionally exempt under section 47B\n(Commonwealth-State relations etc.); and\n(ii) access to the document would, on balance, be contrary\nto the public interest for the purposes of\nsubsection 11A(5).\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt\ndocument unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see\nsection 11A).\nConsultation required\n(2) The agency or Minister must not decide to give the applicant\naccess to the document unless consultation has taken place\nbetween the Commonwealth and the State in accordance with the\narrangements.\nDecision to give access\n(3) If, after such consultation has taken place, the agency or Minister\ndecides to give the applicant access to the document, the agency or\nMinister must give written notice of the decision to both of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the State;\n(b) the applicant.",
      "skos:definition": "relations etc.\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 26A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) arrangements have been entered into between the\nCommonwealth and a State about consultation under this\nsection; and\n(b) a request is made to an agency or Minister for access to a\ndocument that:\n(i) originated with, or was received from, the State or an\nauthority of the State; or\n(ii) contains information (State-originated information)\nthat originated with, or was received from, the State or\nan authority of the State; and\n(c) it appears to the agency or Minister that the State may\nreasonably wish to contend that:\n(i) the document is conditionally exempt under section 47B\n(Commonwealth-State relations etc.); and\n(ii) access to the document would, on balance, be contrary\nto the public interest for the purposes of\nsubsection 11A(5).\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt\ndocument unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see\nsection 11A).\nConsultation required\n(2) The agency or Minister must not decide to give the applicant\naccess to the document unless consultation has taken place\nbetween the Commonwealth and the State in accordance with the\narrangements.\nDecision to give access\n(3) If, after such consultation has taken place, the agency or Minister\ndecides to give the applicant access to the document, the agency or\nMinister must give written notice of the decision to both of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the State;\n(b) the applicant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-26a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-26a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-26a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "25c87689cbac1a668b9cc5fec137a3f37d954f217e5ef666297cde3adfecc603"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-26a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26A Consultation—documents affecting Commonwealth-State",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "relations etc.\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n\nAccess to documents  Part III\n\nSection 26A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) arrangements have been entered into between the\nCommonwealth and a State about consultation under this\nsection; and\n(b) a request is made to an agency or Minister for access to a\ndocument that:\n(i) originated with, or was received from, the State or an\nauthority of the State; or\n(ii) contains information (State-originated information)\nthat originated with, or was received from, the State or\nan authority of the State; and\n(c) it appears to the agency or Minister that the State may\nreasonably wish to contend that:\n(i) the document is conditionally exempt under section 47B\n(Commonwealth-State relations etc.); and\n(ii) access to the document would, on balance, be contrary\nto the public interest for the purposes of\nsubsection 11A(5).\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt\ndocument unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see\nsection 11A).\nConsultation required\n(2) The agency or Minister must not decide to give the applicant\naccess to the document unless consultation has taken place\nbetween the Commonwealth and the State in accordance with the\narrangements.\nDecision to give access\n(3) If, after such consultation has taken place, the agency or Minister\ndecides to give the applicant access to the document, the agency or\nMinister must give written notice of the decision to both of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the State;\n(b) the applicant."
    },
    {
