    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-27a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27A Consultation—documents affecting personal privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-27a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) a request is made to an agency or Minister for access to a\ndocument containing personal information about a person\n(including a person who has died); and\n(b) it appears to the agency or Minister that the person or the\nperson’s legal personal representative (the person\nconcerned) might reasonably wish to make a contention (the\nexemption contention) that:\n(i) the document is conditionally exempt under\nsection 47F; and\n(ii) access to the document would, on balance, be contrary\nto the public interest for the purposes of\nsubsection 11A(5).\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt\ndocument unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see\nsection 11A).\n(2) In determining, for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), whether the\nperson concerned might reasonably wish to make an exemption\ncontention because of personal information in a document, the\nagency or Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n(a) the extent to which the information is well known;\n(b) whether the person to whom the information relates is known\nto be (or to have been) associated with the matters dealt with\nin the information;",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) a request is made to an agency or Minister for access to a\ndocument containing personal information about a person\n(including a person who has died); and\n(b) it appears to the agency or Minister that the person or the\nperson’s legal personal representative (the person\nconcerned) might reasonably wish to make a contention (the\nexemption contention) that:\n(i) the document is conditionally exempt under\nsection 47F; and\n(ii) access to the document would, on balance, be contrary\nto the public interest for the purposes of\nsubsection 11A(5).\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt\ndocument unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see\nsection 11A).\n(2) In determining, for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), whether the\nperson concerned might reasonably wish to make an exemption\ncontention because of personal information in a document, the\nagency or Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n(a) the extent to which the information is well known;\n(b) whether the person to whom the information relates is known\nto be (or to have been) associated with the matters dealt with\nin the information;",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-27a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-27a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-27a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "27A Consultation—documents affecting personal privacy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) a request is made to an agency or Minister for access to a\ndocument containing personal information about a person\n(including a person who has died); and\n(b) it appears to the agency or Minister that the person or the\nperson’s legal personal representative (the person\nconcerned) might reasonably wish to make a contention (the\nexemption contention) that:\n(i) the document is conditionally exempt under\nsection 47F; and\n(ii) access to the document would, on balance, be contrary\nto the public interest for the purposes of\nsubsection 11A(5).\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt\ndocument unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see\nsection 11A).\n(2) In determining, for the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), whether the\nperson concerned might reasonably wish to make an exemption\ncontention because of personal information in a document, the\nagency or Minister must have regard to the following matters:\n(a) the extent to which the information is well known;\n(b) whether the person to whom the information relates is known\nto be (or to have been) associated with the matters dealt with\nin the information;"
    },
