    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, under the regulations, an agency or Minister decides that an\napplicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of a request for access\nto a document, or the provision of access to a document, the\nagency or Minister must give to the applicant a written notice\nstating:\n(a) that the applicant is liable to pay a charge; and\n(b) the agency’s or Minister’s preliminary assessment of the\namount of the charge, and the basis on which the assessment\nis made; and\n(c) that the applicant may contend that the charge has been\nwrongly assessed, or should be reduced or not imposed; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where, under the regulations, an agency or Minister decides that an\napplicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of a request for access\nto a document, or the provision of access to a document, the\nagency or Minister must give to the applicant a written notice\nstating:\n(a) that the applicant is liable to pay a charge; and\n(b) the agency’s or Minister’s preliminary assessment of the\namount of the charge, and the basis on which the assessment\nis made; and\n(c) that the applicant may contend that the charge has been\nwrongly assessed, or should be reduced or not imposed; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-29-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-29-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04f383b8341754280c2ba8af98945f785f864f201b7dbe2af5e6938a277ed178",
      "skos:note": "Agency or Minister must give written notice to applicant stating they are liable to pay a charge.",
      "dc:description": "written notice stating the applicant is liable to pay a charge, preliminary assessment of the amount of the charge, and basis for the assessment"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Charges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, under the regulations, an agency or Minister decides that an\napplicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of a request for access\nto a document, or the provision of access to a document, the\nagency or Minister must give to the applicant a written notice\nstating:\n(a) that the applicant is liable to pay a charge; and\n(b) the agency’s or Minister’s preliminary assessment of the\namount of the charge, and the basis on which the assessment\nis made; and\n(c) that the applicant may contend that the charge has been\nwrongly assessed, or should be reduced or not imposed; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-29-norm",
