      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-33",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33 Documents affecting national security, defence or international",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-33"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "relations\nA document is an exempt document if disclosure of the document\nunder this Act:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth;\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; or\n(b) would divulge any information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an\nauthority of a foreign government or an international\norganization to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an\nauthority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the\ncommunication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an\nauthority of the Commonwealth.\nNote:\nSee also subsection 4(10).",
      "skos:definition": "relations\nA document is an exempt document if disclosure of the document\nunder this Act:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth;\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; or\n(b) would divulge any information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an\nauthority of a foreign government or an international\norganization to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an\nauthority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the\ncommunication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an\nauthority of the Commonwealth.\nNote:\nSee also subsection 4(10).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-33-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-33-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20b78459c063bd881553668a4b544212b27805168c3ec0a54a77c16ead27da97",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of certain documents under this Act is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-33",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33 Documents affecting national security, defence or international",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "relations\nA document is an exempt document if disclosure of the document\nunder this Act:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth;\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; or\n(b) would divulge any information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an\nauthority of a foreign government or an international\norganization to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an\nauthority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the\ncommunication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an\nauthority of the Commonwealth.\nNote:\nSee also subsection 4(10)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-33-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-33"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-33-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 Cabinet documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "General rules\n(1) A document is an exempt document if:\n(a) both of the following are satisfied:\n(i) it has been submitted to the Cabinet for its\nconsideration, or is or was proposed by a Minister to be\nso submitted;\n(ii) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose\nof submission for consideration by the Cabinet; or\n(b) it is an official record of the Cabinet; or\n(c) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of\nbriefing a Minister on a document to which paragraph (a)\napplies; or",
      "skos:definition": "General rules\n(1) A document is an exempt document if:\n(a) both of the following are satisfied:\n(i) it has been submitted to the Cabinet for its\nconsideration, or is or was proposed by a Minister to be\nso submitted;\n(ii) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose\nof submission for consideration by the Cabinet; or\n(b) it is an official record of the Cabinet; or\n(c) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of\nbriefing a Minister on a document to which paragraph (a)\napplies; or",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21b43b56baa49fe6081d71fbca943f3c742bede2e8db0bd58ffdd62cdfa83c4d",
      "skos:note": "A document is exempt if it was submitted to the Cabinet for consideration or proposed by a Minister to be so."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 Cabinet documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "General rules\n(1) A document is an exempt document if:\n(a) both of the following are satisfied:\n(i) it has been submitted to the Cabinet for its\nconsideration, or is or was proposed by a Minister to be\nso submitted;\n(ii) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose\nof submission for consideration by the Cabinet; or\n(b) it is an official record of the Cabinet; or\n(c) it was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of\nbriefing a Minister on a document to which paragraph (a)\napplies; or"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is exempt from",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exempts documents from certain rules",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Cabinet has the power to submit documents for consideration",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Documents submitted or proposed for submission are exempt"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of submission for consideration by the Cabinet",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines when a document is considered exempt due to its creation purpose",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Cabinet has the power to submit documents for consideration",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Documents created with this purpose are exempt"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is or was proposed by a Minister to be submitted",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines when a document is considered exempt due to its proposal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Ministers have the power to propose documents for submission",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Proposed documents are exempt from certain rules"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "was brought into existence for the dominant purpose of briefing a Minister on a document",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines when a document is considered exempt due to its creation purpose",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Ministers have the power to brief each other on documents",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Documents created with this purpose are exempt"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-34-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has been submitted to the Cabinet for its consideration",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines when a document is considered exempt due to its submission",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Cabinet has the power to consider documents",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Submitted documents are exempt from certain rules"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-37",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37 Documents affecting enforcement of law and protection of public",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-37"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.92",
      "values:originalText": "safety\n(1) A document is an exempt document if its disclosure under this Act\nwould, or could reasonably be expected to:\n(a) prejudice the conduct of an investigation of a breach, or\npossible breach, of the law, or a failure, or possible failure, to\ncomply with a law relating to taxation or prejudice the\nenforcement or proper administration of the law in a\nparticular instance;\n\n\nExempt documents  Part IV\nExemptions  Division 2\nSection 38\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(b) disclose, or enable a person to ascertain, the existence or\nidentity of a confidential source of information, or the\nnon-existence of a confidential source of information, in\nrelation to the enforcement or administration of the law; or\n(c) endanger the life or physical safety of any person.\n(2) A document is an exempt document if its disclosure under this Act\nwould, or could reasonably be expected to:\n(a) prejudice the fair trial of a person or the impartial\nadjudication of a particular case;\n(b) disclose lawful methods or procedures for preventing,\ndetecting, investigating, or dealing with matters arising out\nof, breaches or evasions of the law the disclosure of which\nwould, or would be reasonably likely to, prejudice the\neffectiveness of those methods or procedures; or\n(c) prejudice the maintenance or enforcement of lawful methods\nfor the protection of public safety.\n(2A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a person is taken to be a\nconfidential source of information in relation to the enforcement or\nadministration of the law if the person is receiving, or has received,\nprotection under a program conducted under the auspices of the\nAustralian Federal Police, or the police force of a State or\nTerritory, for the protection of:\n(a) witnesses; or\n(b) people who, because of their relationship to, or association\nwith, a witness need, or may need, such protection; or\n(c) any other people who, for any other reason, need or may\nneed, such protection.\n(3) In this section, law means law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "safety\n(1) A document is an exempt document if its disclosure under this Act\nwould, or could reasonably be expected to:\n(a) prejudice the conduct of an investigation of a breach, or\npossible breach, of the law, or a failure, or possible failure, to\ncomply with a law relating to taxation or prejudice the\nenforcement or proper administration of the law in a\nparticular instance;\n\n\nExempt documents  Part IV\nExemptions  Division 2\nSection 38\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(b) disclose, or enable a person to ascertain, the existence or\nidentity of a confidential source of information, or the\nnon-existence of a confidential source of information, in\nrelation to the enforcement or administration of the law; or\n(c) endanger the life or physical safety of any person.\n(2) A document is an exempt document if its disclosure under this Act\nwould, or could reasonably be expected to:\n(a) prejudice the fair trial of a person or the impartial\nadjudication of a particular case;\n(b) disclose lawful methods or procedures for preventing,\ndetecting, investigating, or dealing with matters arising out\nof, breaches or evasions of the law the disclosure of which\nwould, or would be reasonably likely to, prejudice the\neffectiveness of those methods or procedures; or\n(c) prejudice the maintenance or enforcement of lawful methods\nfor the protection of public safety.\n(2A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a person is taken to be a\nconfidential source of information in relation to the enforcement or\nadministration of the law if the person is receiving, or has received,\nprotection under a program conducted under the auspices of the\nAustralian Federal Police, or the police force of a State or\nTerritory, for the protection of:\n(a) witnesses; or\n(b) people who, because of their relationship to, or association\nwith, a witness need, or may need, such protection; or\n(c) any other people who, for any other reason, need or may\nneed, such protection.\n(3) In this section, law",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-37-ss-1"
        },
