      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c2434b0b66c9d2c4d50fd3bc3dfc96f399bb907682d93611ca8dc987f3005ab1",
      "skos:note": "Person receiving protection under a program is considered confidential source of information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-37-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37(2A) Documents affecting enforcement of law and protection of public",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 92,
      "values:originalText": "(2A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a person is taken to be a\nconfidential source of information in relation to the enforcement or\nadministration of the law if the person is receiving, or has received,\nprotection under a program conducted under the auspices of the\nAustralian Federal Police, or the police force of a State or\nTerritory, for the protection of:\n(a) witnesses; or\n(b) people who, because of their relationship to, or association\nwith, a witness need, or may need, such protection; or\n(c) any other people who, for any other reason, need or may\nneed, such protection."
    },
    {
