    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47A Electoral rolls and related documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\nElectoral Act means the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918.\nelectoral roll means:\n(a) a Roll of the electors of:\n(i) a State or Territory; or\n(ii) a Division (within the meaning of the Electoral Act); or\n(iii) a Subdivision (within the meaning of the Electoral Act);\nprepared under the Electoral Act; or\n(b) any part of a Roll referred to in paragraph (a).\n(2) Subject to this section, a document is an exempt document if it is:\n(a) an electoral roll; or\n(b) a print, or a copy of a print, of an electoral roll; or\n(c) a microfiche of an electoral roll; or\n(d) a copy on tape or disk of an electoral roll; or\n(e) a document that:\n(i) sets out particulars of only one elector; and\n(ii) was used to prepare an electoral roll; or\n(f) a document that:\n(i) is a copy of a document referred to in paragraph (e); or\n(ii) contains only copies of documents referred to in\nparagraph (e); or\n(g) a document (including a habitation index within the meaning\nof the Electoral Act) that:\n(i) sets out particulars of electors; and\n(ii) was derived from an electoral roll.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this section:\nElectoral Act means the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918.\nelectoral roll means:\n(a) a Roll of the electors of:\n(i) a State or Territory; or\n(ii) a Division (within the meaning of the Electoral Act); or\n(iii) a Subdivision (within the meaning of the Electoral Act);\nprepared under the Electoral Act; or\n(b) any part of a Roll referred to in paragraph (a).\n(2) Subject to this section, a document is an exempt document if it is:\n(a) an electoral roll; or\n(b) a print, or a copy of a print, of an electoral roll; or\n(c) a microfiche of an electoral roll; or\n(d) a copy on tape or disk of an electoral roll; or\n(e) a document that:\n(i) sets out particulars of only one elector; and\n(ii) was used to prepare an electoral roll; or\n(f) a document that:\n(i) is a copy of a document referred to in paragraph (e); or\n(ii) contains only copies of documents referred to in\nparagraph (e); or\n(g) a document (including a habitation index within the meaning\nof the Electoral Act) that:\n(i) sets out particulars of electors; and\n(ii) was derived from an electoral roll.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f1bb5131e5ab0a17d7f7a32f07995669addb65e341f82c15fd1e83e2e6efdb09"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47A Electoral rolls and related documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 99,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\nElectoral Act means the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918.\nelectoral roll means:\n(a) a Roll of the electors of:\n(i) a State or Territory; or\n(ii) a Division (within the meaning of the Electoral Act); or\n(iii) a Subdivision (within the meaning of the Electoral Act);\nprepared under the Electoral Act; or\n(b) any part of a Roll referred to in paragraph (a).\n(2) Subject to this section, a document is an exempt document if it is:\n(a) an electoral roll; or\n(b) a print, or a copy of a print, of an electoral roll; or\n(c) a microfiche of an electoral roll; or\n(d) a copy on tape or disk of an electoral roll; or\n(e) a document that:\n(i) sets out particulars of only one elector; and\n(ii) was used to prepare an electoral roll; or\n(f) a document that:\n(i) is a copy of a document referred to in paragraph (e); or\n(ii) contains only copies of documents referred to in\nparagraph (e); or\n(g) a document (including a habitation index within the meaning\nof the Electoral Act) that:\n(i) sets out particulars of electors; and\n(ii) was derived from an electoral roll."
    },
