      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "a document that was used to prepare an electoral roll; or a document that is a copy of a document referred to in paragraph (e)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "or any other document that meets these criteria"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47a-ss-2-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "and",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Describes the conditions under which documents are exempt",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) sets out particulars of only one elector; and (ii) was used to prepare an electoral roll",
      "cml:conclusionText": "or any other document that meets these criteria"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47a-ss-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "includes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Lists additional examples of exempt documents",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) is a copy of a document referred to in paragraph (e); or (ii) contains only copies of documents referred to in paragraph (e)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "or any other document that meets these criteria"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47B Public interest conditional exemptions—Commonwealth-State",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "relations etc.\nA document is conditionally exempt if disclosure of the document\nunder this Act:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to\nrelations between the Commonwealth and a State; or\n(b) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of the Government of a State or\nan authority of a State, to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth; or\n(d) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a Norfolk Island authority, to\nthe Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the\nCommonwealth or to a person receiving the communication\non behalf of the Commonwealth or an authority of the\nCommonwealth; or\n(f) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of the Government of a State or\nan authority of a State, to a Norfolk Island authority or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of a Norfolk\nIsland authority.\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document\nunless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A).",
      "skos:definition": "relations etc.\nA document is conditionally exempt if disclosure of the document\nunder this Act:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to\nrelations between the Commonwealth and a State; or\n(b) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of the Government of a State or\nan authority of a State, to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth; or\n(d) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a Norfolk Island authority, to\nthe Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the\nCommonwealth or to a person receiving the communication\non behalf of the Commonwealth or an authority of the\nCommonwealth; or\n(f) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of the Government of a State or\nan authority of a State, to a Norfolk Island authority or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of a Norfolk\nIsland authority.\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document\nunless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df663c9d1f8fb6aa3b0592f20b26e77d886dd67573086f691cff7ce1bdbd3da3",
      "skos:note": "Conditional exemptions for public interest"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47B Public interest conditional exemptions—Commonwealth-State",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "relations etc.\nA document is conditionally exempt if disclosure of the document\nunder this Act:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to\nrelations between the Commonwealth and a State; or\n(b) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of the Government of a State or\nan authority of a State, to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth; or\n(d) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of a Norfolk Island authority, to\nthe Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the\nCommonwealth or to a person receiving the communication\non behalf of the Commonwealth or an authority of the\nCommonwealth; or\n(f) would divulge information or matter communicated in\nconfidence by or on behalf of the Government of a State or\nan authority of a State, to a Norfolk Island authority or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of a Norfolk\nIsland authority.\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document\nunless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47b"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47b-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Public interest exemption",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Disclosure would cause damage to relations between the Commonwealth and a State",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption granted"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47C Public interest conditional exemptions—deliberative processes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "General rule\n(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould disclose matter (deliberative matter) in the nature of, or\nrelating to, opinion, advice or recommendation obtained, prepared",
      "skos:definition": "General rule\n(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould disclose matter (deliberative matter) in the nature of, or\nrelating to, opinion, advice or recommendation obtained, prepared",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47c-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "007a8e21262be88c90835848946736ba7b14dc8e1439cbb7ce8bfd778ed9f4b0",
      "skos:note": "Conditional exemptions for deliberative processes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47C Public interest conditional exemptions—deliberative processes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "General rule\n(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould disclose matter (deliberative matter) in the nature of, or\nrelating to, opinion, advice or recommendation obtained, prepared"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47c-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47c"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47D Public interest conditional exemptions—financial or property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "interests of the Commonwealth\nA document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould have a substantial adverse effect on the financial or property\ninterests of the Commonwealth or of an agency.\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document\nunless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A).\n\n\nExempt documents  Part IV\nPublic interest conditional exemptions  Division 3\nSection 47E\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "interests of the Commonwealth\nA document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould have a substantial adverse effect on the financial or property\ninterests of the Commonwealth or of an agency.\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document\nunless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A).\n\n\nExempt documents  Part IV\nPublic interest conditional exemptions  Division 3\nSection 47E\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47d-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47d-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e82dd04a3189388d2736469b6ad3fa511f5f28730f23067c0bcec0a45b2d671b",
      "skos:note": "Conditional exemptions for documents with substantial adverse effect on Commonwealth or agency interests."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47D Public interest conditional exemptions—financial or property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "interests of the Commonwealth\nA document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould have a substantial adverse effect on the financial or property\ninterests of the Commonwealth or of an agency.\nNote:\nAccess must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document\nunless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A).\n\n\nExempt documents  Part IV\nPublic interest conditional exemptions  Division 3\nSection 47E\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
