      },
      "cml:operator": "Spreads",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The agency must consider how the disclosure of the document would affect the person's privacy.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the extent to which the information is well known;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the availability of the information from publicly accessible sources;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47f-ss-2-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognizes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The agency must recognize the importance of personal privacy in its decision-making.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) In determining whether the disclosure of the document would involve the unreasonable disclosure of personal information, an agency or Minister must have regard to...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the person to whom the information relates is known to be (or to have been) associated with the matters dealt with in the document;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47G Public interest conditional exemptions—business",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-47g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.105",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould disclose information concerning a person in respect of his or\nher business or professional affairs or concerning the business,\ncommercial or financial affairs of an organisation or undertaking,\nin a case in which the disclosure of the information:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, unreasonably\naffect that person adversely in respect of his or her lawful\nbusiness or professional affairs or that organisation or\nundertaking in respect of its lawful business, commercial or\nfinancial affairs; or\n(b) could reasonably be expected to prejudice the future supply\nof information to the Commonwealth or an agency for the\npurpose of the administration of a law of the Commonwealth\nor of a Territory or the administration of matters\nadministered by an agency.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to trade secrets or other information\nto which section 47 applies.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not have effect in relation to a request by a\nperson for access to a document:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould disclose information concerning a person in respect of his or\nher business or professional affairs or concerning the business,\ncommercial or financial affairs of an organisation or undertaking,\nin a case in which the disclosure of the information:\n(a) would, or could reasonably be expected to, unreasonably\naffect that person adversely in respect of his or her lawful\nbusiness or professional affairs or that organisation or\nundertaking in respect of its lawful business, commercial or\nfinancial affairs; or\n(b) could reasonably be expected to prejudice the future supply\nof information to the Commonwealth or an agency for the\npurpose of the administration of a law of the Commonwealth\nor of a Territory or the administration of matters\nadministered by an agency.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to trade secrets or other information\nto which section 47 applies.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not have effect in relation to a request by a\nperson for access to a document:",
