      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.107",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould, or could be reasonably expected to, have a substantial\nadverse effect on Australia’s economy by:\n(a) influencing a decision or action of a person or entity; or\n(b) giving a person (or class of persons) an undue benefit or\ndetriment, in relation to business carried on by the person (or\nclass), by providing premature knowledge of proposed or\npossible action or inaction of a person or entity.\nNote:\nA person includes a body corporate and a body politic (see\nsubsection 2C(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901). Examples of a\nbody politic include the government of the Commonwealth, a State, a\nTerritory or a foreign country.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act\nwould, or could be reasonably expected to, have a substantial\nadverse effect on Australia’s economy by:\n(a) influencing a decision or action of a person or entity; or\n(b) giving a person (or class of persons) an undue benefit or\ndetriment, in relation to business carried on by the person (or\nclass), by providing premature knowledge of proposed or\npossible action or inaction of a person or entity.\nNote:\nA person includes a body corporate and a body politic (see\nsubsection 2C(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901). Examples of a\nbody politic include the government of the Commonwealth, a State, a\nTerritory or a foreign country.",
