      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 Amendment of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to section 51C, where the agency or Minister to whom\nsuch an application is made is satisfied that:\n(a) the record of personal information to which the request\nrelates is contained in a document of the agency or an official\ndocument of the Minister, as the case may be; and\n(b) the information is incomplete, incorrect, out of date or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the information has been used, is being used or is available\nfor use by the agency or Minister for an administrative\npurpose;\nthe agency or Minister may amend the record of information.\n(2) The agency or Minister may make the amendment:\n(a) by altering the document or official document concerned to\nmake the information complete, correct, up to date or not\nmisleading; or\n(b) by adding to that document or official document a note:\n(i) specifying the respects in which the agency or Minister\nis satisfied that the information is incomplete, incorrect,\nout of date or misleading; and\n(ii) in a case where the agency or Minister is satisfied that\nthe information is out of date—setting out such\ninformation as is required to bring the information up to\ndate.\n(3) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the agency or Minister\nmust, when making an amendment under paragraph (2)(a), ensure\nthat the record of information is amended in a way that does not\n\n\nAmendment and annotation of personal records  Part V\n\nSection 51\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nobliterate the text of the record as it existed prior to the\namendment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to section 51C, where the agency or Minister to whom\nsuch an application is made is satisfied that:\n(a) the record of personal information to which the request\nrelates is contained in a document of the agency or an official\ndocument of the Minister, as the case may be; and\n(b) the information is incomplete, incorrect, out of date or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the information has been used, is being used or is available\nfor use by the agency or Minister for an administrative\npurpose;\nthe agency or Minister may amend the record of information.\n(2) The agency or Minister may make the amendment:\n(a) by altering the document or official document concerned to\nmake the information complete, correct, up to date or not\nmisleading; or\n(b) by adding to that document or official document a note:\n(i) specifying the respects in which the agency or Minister\nis satisfied that the information is incomplete, incorrect,\nout of date or misleading; and\n(ii) in a case where the agency or Minister is satisfied that\nthe information is out of date—setting out such\ninformation as is required to bring the information up to\ndate.\n(3) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the agency or Minister\nmust, when making an amendment under paragraph (2)(a), ensure\nthat the record of information is amended in a way that does not\n\n\nAmendment and annotation of personal records  Part V\n\nSection 51\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nobliterate the text of the record as it existed prior to the\namendment.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "544fec87698b9b57983c61eac4f0b8b1d861cdac68aa23bfec617ca8f8674489"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 Amendment of records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to section 51C, where the agency or Minister to whom\nsuch an application is made is satisfied that:\n(a) the record of personal information to which the request\nrelates is contained in a document of the agency or an official\ndocument of the Minister, as the case may be; and\n(b) the information is incomplete, incorrect, out of date or\nmisleading; and\n(c) the information has been used, is being used or is available\nfor use by the agency or Minister for an administrative\npurpose;\nthe agency or Minister may amend the record of information.\n(2) The agency or Minister may make the amendment:\n(a) by altering the document or official document concerned to\nmake the information complete, correct, up to date or not\nmisleading; or\n(b) by adding to that document or official document a note:\n(i) specifying the respects in which the agency or Minister\nis satisfied that the information is incomplete, incorrect,\nout of date or misleading; and\n(ii) in a case where the agency or Minister is satisfied that\nthe information is out of date—setting out such\ninformation as is required to bring the information up to\ndate.\n(3) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the agency or Minister\nmust, when making an amendment under paragraph (2)(a), ensure\nthat the record of information is amended in a way that does not\n\n\nAmendment and annotation of personal records  Part V\n\nSection 51\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nobliterate the text of the record as it existed prior to the\namendment."
    },
