      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The agency or Minister may make the amendment:\n(a) by altering the document or official document concerned to\nmake the information complete, correct, up to date or not\nmisleading; or\n(b) by adding to that document or official document a note:\n(i) specifying the respects in which the agency or Minister\nis satisfied that the information is incomplete, incorrect,\nout of date or misleading; and\n(ii) in a case where the agency or Minister is satisfied that\nthe information is out of date—setting out such\ninformation as is required to bring the information up to\ndate.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The agency or Minister may make the amendment:\n(a) by altering the document or official document concerned to\nmake the information complete, correct, up to date or not\nmisleading; or\n(b) by adding to that document or official document a note:\n(i) specifying the respects in which the agency or Minister\nis satisfied that the information is incomplete, incorrect,\nout of date or misleading; and\n(ii) in a case where the agency or Minister is satisfied that\nthe information is out of date—setting out such\ninformation as is required to bring the information up to\ndate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "94def94a6c9db2abf730405d0bedc47f921fb9851e232ce2797af9f96b4c278f",
      "skos:note": "Agency or Minister may make amendment to records."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-50-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50(2) Amendment of records",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The agency or Minister may make the amendment:\n(a) by altering the document or official document concerned to\nmake the information complete, correct, up to date or not\nmisleading; or\n(b) by adding to that document or official document a note:\n(i) specifying the respects in which the agency or Minister\nis satisfied that the information is incomplete, incorrect,\nout of date or misleading; and\n(ii) in a case where the agency or Minister is satisfied that\nthe information is out of date—setting out such\ninformation as is required to bring the information up to\ndate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-50-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50(3) Amendment of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-50-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
