    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Annotations of records etc. following unsuccessful applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.111",
      "values:originalText": "for amendments of records\n(1) Where an agency or Minister decides not to amend a document or\nofficial documents wholly or partly in accordance with an\napplication under section 48, the agency or Minister must:\n(a) take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to\nenable the applicant to provide a statement of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph 51A(c); and\n(b) subject to subsection (2), annotate the document or official\ndocument concerned by adding to it the statement so\nprovided.\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply if the agency or Minister considers\nthe statement to be irrelevant, defamatory or unnecessarily\nvoluminous.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act, the provision by the applicant of a\nstatement under subsection (1) is taken to be an application made\nunder section 51A on the day the statement is so provided.",
      "skos:definition": "for amendments of records\n(1) Where an agency or Minister decides not to amend a document or\nofficial documents wholly or partly in accordance with an\napplication under section 48, the agency or Minister must:\n(a) take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to\nenable the applicant to provide a statement of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph 51A(c); and\n(b) subject to subsection (2), annotate the document or official\ndocument concerned by adding to it the statement so\nprovided.\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply if the agency or Minister considers\nthe statement to be irrelevant, defamatory or unnecessarily\nvoluminous.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act, the provision by the applicant of a\nstatement under subsection (1) is taken to be an application made\nunder section 51A on the day the statement is so provided.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7484e623465b2398cb33c88d64787af8257c1bb43257862c9476bcb781eeb53"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Annotations of records etc. following unsuccessful applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 111,
      "values:originalText": "for amendments of records\n(1) Where an agency or Minister decides not to amend a document or\nofficial documents wholly or partly in accordance with an\napplication under section 48, the agency or Minister must:\n(a) take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to\nenable the applicant to provide a statement of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph 51A(c); and\n(b) subject to subsection (2), annotate the document or official\ndocument concerned by adding to it the statement so\nprovided.\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply if the agency or Minister considers\nthe statement to be irrelevant, defamatory or unnecessarily\nvoluminous.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act, the provision by the applicant of a\nstatement under subsection (1) is taken to be an application made\nunder section 51A on the day the statement is so provided."
    },
