    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51D Notification etc. of a decision under this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-51d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an application is made to an agency or Minister under this\nPart, the agency or Minister must take all reasonable steps to\nenable the applicant to be notified of a decision on the application\nas soon as practicable but in any case not later than 30 days after\nthe day on which the request is received by or on behalf of the\nagency or Minister.\n(2) Section 23 applies in relation to a decision on an application made\nunder section 48.\n(3) Section 26 applies in relation to a decision made under this\nPart refusing to amend or annotate a record as if that decision were\na decision made under Part III refusing to grant access to a\ndocument in accordance with a request made under\nsubsection 15(1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where an application is made to an agency or Minister under this\nPart, the agency or Minister must take all reasonable steps to\nenable the applicant to be notified of a decision on the application\nas soon as practicable but in any case not later than 30 days after\nthe day on which the request is received by or on behalf of the\nagency or Minister.\n(2) Section 23 applies in relation to a decision on an application made\nunder section 48.\n(3) Section 26 applies in relation to a decision made under this\nPart refusing to amend or annotate a record as if that decision were\na decision made under Part III refusing to grant access to a\ndocument in accordance with a request made under\nsubsection 15(1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-51d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d184f3a5f2153c15e25bf920c0f14c806e94fe61078452a0b955807d656d948"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-51d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51D Notification etc. of a decision under this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where an application is made to an agency or Minister under this\nPart, the agency or Minister must take all reasonable steps to\nenable the applicant to be notified of a decision on the application\nas soon as practicable but in any case not later than 30 days after\nthe day on which the request is received by or on behalf of the\nagency or Minister.\n(2) Section 23 applies in relation to a decision on an application made\nunder section 48.\n(3) Section 26 applies in relation to a decision made under this\nPart refusing to amend or annotate a record as if that decision were\na decision made under Part III refusing to grant access to a\ndocument in accordance with a request made under\nsubsection 15(1)."
    },
