    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-53b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53B What is an access grant decision?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-53b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.119",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An access grant decision is a decision covered by the following\ntable:\nNote:\nThe table covers documents that may be conditionally exempt under\nsection 47B (items 1 and 1A), 47G (item 2) or 47F (items 3 and 4), or\nexempt under section 47 (item 2). Access must generally be given to a\nconditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the\npublic interest (see section 11A).\nAccess grant decisions\nItem\nIf, in relation to a request for\naccess to a document ...\nthe access grant decision is ...\nconsultation with a State under\nsection 26A (documents\naffecting Commonwealth-State\nrelations etc.) is required\na decision of an agency or Minister to give\nthe applicant access to the document (or an\nedited copy of the document) because:\n(a) the document is not conditionally\nexempt under section 47B\n(Commonwealth-State relations etc.);\nor",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An access grant decision is a decision covered by the following\ntable:\nNote:\nThe table covers documents that may be conditionally exempt under\nsection 47B (items 1 and 1A), 47G (item 2) or 47F (items 3 and 4), or\nexempt under section 47 (item 2). Access must generally be given to a\nconditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the\npublic interest (see section 11A).\nAccess grant decisions\nItem\nIf, in relation to a request for\naccess to a document ...\nthe access grant decision is ...\nconsultation with a State under\nsection 26A (documents\naffecting Commonwealth-State\nrelations etc.) is required\na decision of an agency or Minister to give\nthe applicant access to the document (or an\nedited copy of the document) because:\n(a) the document is not conditionally\nexempt under section 47B\n(Commonwealth-State relations etc.);\nor",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-53b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-53b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5c510d8f5ad6aac8127d501b9f84b8d994678f32da0aa26121d9d5e8157d9065",
      "skos:note": "Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-53b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53B What is an access grant decision?",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 119,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An access grant decision is a decision covered by the following\ntable:\nNote:\nThe table covers documents that may be conditionally exempt under\nsection 47B (items 1 and 1A), 47G (item 2) or 47F (items 3 and 4), or\nexempt under section 47 (item 2). Access must generally be given to a\nconditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the\npublic interest (see section 11A).\nAccess grant decisions\nItem\nIf, in relation to a request for\naccess to a document ...\nthe access grant decision is ...\nconsultation with a State under\nsection 26A (documents\naffecting Commonwealth-State\nrelations etc.) is required\na decision of an agency or Minister to give\nthe applicant access to the document (or an\nedited copy of the document) because:\n(a) the document is not conditionally\nexempt under section 47B\n(Commonwealth-State relations etc.);\nor"
    },
