    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54K Key concepts—what is an IC reviewable decision?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "An IC reviewable decision is:\n(a) a decision covered by subsection 54L(2) (access refusal\ndecisions); or\n(b) a decision covered by subsection 54M(2) (access grant\ndecisions).\nNote:\nIC reviewable decision is short for Information Commissioner\nreviewable decision.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nIC reviewable decisions  Division 3\nSection 54L\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "An IC reviewable decision is:\n(a) a decision covered by subsection 54L(2) (access refusal\ndecisions); or\n(b) a decision covered by subsection 54M(2) (access grant\ndecisions).\nNote:\nIC reviewable decision is short for Information Commissioner\nreviewable decision.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nIC reviewable decisions  Division 3\nSection 54L\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54k-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "645673e55d7ab6b1a05075c39f38a15f778f085ff04cb57f562e8f67282150b8",
      "skos:note": "Defines IC reviewable decision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54K Key concepts—what is an IC reviewable decision?",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "An IC reviewable decision is:\n(a) a decision covered by subsection 54L(2) (access refusal\ndecisions); or\n(b) a decision covered by subsection 54M(2) (access grant\ndecisions).\nNote:\nIC reviewable decision is short for Information Commissioner\nreviewable decision.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nIC reviewable decisions  Division 3\nSection 54L\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54k-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54k"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54L IC reviewable decisions—access refusal decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application may be made to the Information Commissioner for\na review of a decision covered by subsection (2).\n(2) This subsection covers the following decisions:\n(a) an access refusal decision;\n(b) a decision made by an agency on internal review of an access\nrefusal decision (see section 54C);\n(c) a decision refusing to allow a further period for making an\napplication for internal review of an access refusal decision\n(under section 54B).\nNote 1:\nAn application for the review of an access refusal decision made for\nthe purposes of paragraph (a) may be made regardless of whether the\ndecision was the subject of internal review.\nNote 2:\nIf no decision is made on internal review within 30 days, a decision to\naffirm the original access refusal decision is taken to have been made\n(see section 54D).\n(3) The IC review application may be made by, or on behalf of, the\nperson who made the request to which the decision relates.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application may be made to the Information Commissioner for\na review of a decision covered by subsection (2).\n(2) This subsection covers the following decisions:\n(a) an access refusal decision;\n(b) a decision made by an agency on internal review of an access\nrefusal decision (see section 54C);\n(c) a decision refusing to allow a further period for making an\napplication for internal review of an access refusal decision\n(under section 54B).\nNote 1:\nAn application for the review of an access refusal decision made for\nthe purposes of paragraph (a) may be made regardless of whether the\ndecision was the subject of internal review.\nNote 2:\nIf no decision is made on internal review within 30 days, a decision to\naffirm the original access refusal decision is taken to have been made\n(see section 54D).\n(3) The IC review application may be made by, or on behalf of, the\nperson who made the request to which the decision relates.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ac73b9cbb7aaecc29612b47216f3c523d70a4479e7fe990d1543c1b7e721f60c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54L IC reviewable decisions—access refusal decisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application may be made to the Information Commissioner for\na review of a decision covered by subsection (2).\n(2) This subsection covers the following decisions:\n(a) an access refusal decision;\n(b) a decision made by an agency on internal review of an access\nrefusal decision (see section 54C);\n(c) a decision refusing to allow a further period for making an\napplication for internal review of an access refusal decision\n(under section 54B).\nNote 1:\nAn application for the review of an access refusal decision made for\nthe purposes of paragraph (a) may be made regardless of whether the\ndecision was the subject of internal review.\nNote 2:\nIf no decision is made on internal review within 30 days, a decision to\naffirm the original access refusal decision is taken to have been made\n(see section 54D).\n(3) The IC review application may be made by, or on behalf of, the\nperson who made the request to which the decision relates."
    },
    {
