    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54P IC review applications—requirement to notify affected third",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "parties\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister decides not to give access to a\ndocument to which a consultation requirement applies under\nsection 26A, 27 or 27A; and\n(b) an IC review application is made for an IC review of that\ndecision.\nRequirement to notify\n(2) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, take all\nreasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the document\nof the application.\nNote 1:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.\nNote 2:\nThe agency or Minister is not required to give notice if the\nInformation Commissioner orders that it is not appropriate to do so in\nthe circumstances (see section 54Q).\n(3) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, give a copy of\nthe notice to the Information Commissioner.",
      "skos:definition": "parties\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister decides not to give access to a\ndocument to which a consultation requirement applies under\nsection 26A, 27 or 27A; and\n(b) an IC review application is made for an IC review of that\ndecision.\nRequirement to notify\n(2) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, take all\nreasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the document\nof the application.\nNote 1:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.\nNote 2:\nThe agency or Minister is not required to give notice if the\nInformation Commissioner orders that it is not appropriate to do so in\nthe circumstances (see section 54Q).\n(3) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, give a copy of\nthe notice to the Information Commissioner.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54p-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3e77857035d342cc37b8700be499cb2a22516a626e6ea7fe72c995ed6d6f8248"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54P IC review applications—requirement to notify affected third",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "parties\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister decides not to give access to a\ndocument to which a consultation requirement applies under\nsection 26A, 27 or 27A; and\n(b) an IC review application is made for an IC review of that\ndecision.\nRequirement to notify\n(2) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, take all\nreasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the document\nof the application.\nNote 1:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.\nNote 2:\nThe agency or Minister is not required to give notice if the\nInformation Commissioner orders that it is not appropriate to do so in\nthe circumstances (see section 54Q).\n(3) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, give a copy of\nthe notice to the Information Commissioner."
    },
