    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54q-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54Q(3) IC review applications—circumstances in which not giving",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54q-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The circumstances covered by this subsection are whether\nnotifying the affected third party would, or could reasonably be\nexpected to, do any of the following:\n(a) prejudice the conduct of an investigation of a breach, or\npossible breach, of the law, or a failure, or possible failure, to\ncomply with a law relating to taxation;\n(b) prejudice the enforcement or proper administration of the law\nin a particular instance;\n(c) disclose, or enable a person to ascertain, the existence or\nidentity of a confidential source of information, or the\nnon-existence of a confidential source of information, in\nrelation to the enforcement or administration of the law;\n(d) endanger the life or physical safety of any person;\n(e) cause damage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The circumstances covered by this subsection are whether\nnotifying the affected third party would, or could reasonably be\nexpected to, do any of the following:\n(a) prejudice the conduct of an investigation of a breach, or\npossible breach, of the law, or a failure, or possible failure, to\ncomply with a law relating to taxation;\n(b) prejudice the enforcement or proper administration of the law\nin a particular instance;\n(c) disclose, or enable a person to ascertain, the existence or\nidentity of a confidential source of information, or the\nnon-existence of a confidential source of information, in\nrelation to the enforcement or administration of the law;\n(d) endanger the life or physical safety of any person;\n(e) cause damage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54q-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54q-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cada1f2bcda1e1900c3ca6b66ca14f967dc434bb1fe26e49ecceb0822bfd2276",
      "skos:note": "Notifying an affected third party would prejudice certain activities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54q-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54Q(3) IC review applications—circumstances in which not giving",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The circumstances covered by this subsection are whether\nnotifying the affected third party would, or could reasonably be\nexpected to, do any of the following:\n(a) prejudice the conduct of an investigation of a breach, or\npossible breach, of the law, or a failure, or possible failure, to\ncomply with a law relating to taxation;\n(b) prejudice the enforcement or proper administration of the law\nin a particular instance;\n(c) disclose, or enable a person to ascertain, the existence or\nidentity of a confidential source of information, or the\nnon-existence of a confidential source of information, in\nrelation to the enforcement or administration of the law;\n(d) endanger the life or physical safety of any person;\n(e) cause damage to the security, defence or international\nrelations of the Commonwealth."
    },
