    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54x",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54X Decision to review—notice requirement if discretion not to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54x"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.137",
      "values:originalText": "review exercised\n(1) This section applies if the Information Commissioner decides not\nto undertake an IC review, or not to continue to undertake an IC\nreview.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, notify\nthe review parties of the decision in writing.\n(3) The notice must:\n(a) state the reasons for the Information Commissioner’s\ndecision; and\n(b) if the Information Commissioner makes a decision under\nparagraph 54W(b)—state that an application for review of\nthe relevant IC reviewable decision may be made to the\nTribunal under section 57A.\nNote:\nSee section 57A for the time within which the application for review\nmust be made to the Tribunal.\n(4) However, the notice must not include:\n(a) exempt matter; or\n(b) information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1).\nNote:\nSubsection 25(1) deals with information about the existence or\notherwise of certain documents.",
      "skos:definition": "review exercised\n(1) This section applies if the Information Commissioner decides not\nto undertake an IC review, or not to continue to undertake an IC\nreview.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, notify\nthe review parties of the decision in writing.\n(3) The notice must:\n(a) state the reasons for the Information Commissioner’s\ndecision; and\n(b) if the Information Commissioner makes a decision under\nparagraph 54W(b)—state that an application for review of\nthe relevant IC reviewable decision may be made to the\nTribunal under section 57A.\nNote:\nSee section 57A for the time within which the application for review\nmust be made to the Tribunal.\n(4) However, the notice must not include:\n(a) exempt matter; or\n(b) information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1).\nNote:\nSubsection 25(1) deals with information about the existence or\notherwise of certain documents.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54x-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54x-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54x-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54x-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d017c8beca4210ba589e7e1e2556df09c8201c5d803b483859f13c7c565ec7ac"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54x",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54X Decision to review—notice requirement if discretion not to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 137,
      "values:originalText": "review exercised\n(1) This section applies if the Information Commissioner decides not\nto undertake an IC review, or not to continue to undertake an IC\nreview.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must, as soon as practicable, notify\nthe review parties of the decision in writing.\n(3) The notice must:\n(a) state the reasons for the Information Commissioner’s\ndecision; and\n(b) if the Information Commissioner makes a decision under\nparagraph 54W(b)—state that an application for review of\nthe relevant IC reviewable decision may be made to the\nTribunal under section 57A.\nNote:\nSee section 57A for the time within which the application for review\nmust be made to the Tribunal.\n(4) However, the notice must not include:\n(a) exempt matter; or\n(b) information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1).\nNote:\nSubsection 25(1) deals with information about the existence or\notherwise of certain documents."
    },
