    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54Y Decision to review—actual decisions made after IC review has",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "commenced\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister has been taken to have made a decision\n(the deemed decision) under subsection 15AC(3),\n51DA(2) or 54D(2); and\n(b) a person makes an IC review application for review of the\ndeemed decision; and\n(c) the Information Commissioner has not made a decision under\nsection 54W (decision not to review) or 55K (decision on\nreview) in relation to the deemed decision; and\n(d) subsection 15AC(7), 51DA(6) or 54D(6) applies in relation\nto a decision (the actual decision) made by the agency or\nMinister.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must deal with the IC review\napplication for review of the deemed decision as if it were an IC\nreview application for the review of the actual decision, subject\notherwise to this Part.\nNote:\nWhen making the actual decision, a consultation requirement under\nsection 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations\netc.), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal\nprivacy) may apply.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nProcedure in IC review  Division 6\nSection 54Z\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "commenced\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) an agency or Minister has been taken to have made a decision\n(the deemed decision) under subsection 15AC(3),\n51DA(2) or 54D(2); and\n(b) a person makes an IC review application for review of the\ndeemed decision; and\n(c) the Information Commissioner has not made a decision under\nsection 54W (decision not to review) or 55K (decision on\nreview) in relation to the deemed decision; and\n(d) subsection 15AC(7), 51DA(6) or 54D(6) applies in relation\nto a decision (the actual decision) made by the agency or\nMinister.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must deal with the IC review\napplication for review of the deemed decision as if it were an IC\nreview application for the review of the actual decision, subject\notherwise to this Part.\nNote:\nWhen making the actual decision, a consultation requirement under\nsection 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations\netc.), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal\nprivacy) may apply.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nProcedure in IC review  Division 6\nSection 54Z\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54y-ss-1"
        },
