    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54Z Procedure in IC review—general notice requirement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "Before undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust inform:\n(a) the person, agency or Minister who made the decision; or\n(b) if the IC review application is made under section 54M\n(access grant decisions)—the person who made the request.",
      "skos:definition": "Before undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust inform:\n(a) the person, agency or Minister who made the decision; or\n(b) if the IC review application is made under section 54M\n(access grant decisions)—the person who made the request.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54z-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54z-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d6c4f6d7bf11ff690d11b78053affa7e908bbc72e2819004310f9e4e2e2cde40",
      "skos:note": "Information Commissioner must inform person, agency or Minister who made the decision before undertaking IC review."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-54z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54Z Procedure in IC review—general notice requirement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "Before undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust inform:\n(a) the person, agency or Minister who made the decision; or\n(b) if the IC review application is made under section 54M\n(access grant decisions)—the person who made the request."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54z-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54z"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54z-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to inform",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Procedure in IC review—general",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, for the purposes of an IC\nreview, review an IC reviewable decision by considering the\ndocuments or other material lodged with or provided to the\nInformation Commissioner, and without holding a hearing, if:\n(a) it appears to the Information Commissioner that the issues\nfor determination on the IC review can be adequately\ndetermined in the absence of the review parties; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner is satisfied that there are no\nunusual circumstances that would warrant the Information\nCommissioner holding a hearing; and\n(c) none of the review parties have applied for a hearing under\nsection 55B.\n(2) The Information Commissioner may otherwise:\n(a) conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers\nappropriate; and\n(b) use any technique that the Information Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate to facilitate an agreed resolution of\nmatters at issue in the IC review (for example by using\ntechniques that are used in alternative dispute resolution\nprocesses); and\n(c) allow a person to participate in an IC review by any means of\ncommunication; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, for the purposes of an IC\nreview, review an IC reviewable decision by considering the\ndocuments or other material lodged with or provided to the\nInformation Commissioner, and without holding a hearing, if:\n(a) it appears to the Information Commissioner that the issues\nfor determination on the IC review can be adequately\ndetermined in the absence of the review parties; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner is satisfied that there are no\nunusual circumstances that would warrant the Information\nCommissioner holding a hearing; and\n(c) none of the review parties have applied for a hearing under\nsection 55B.\n(2) The Information Commissioner may otherwise:\n(a) conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers\nappropriate; and\n(b) use any technique that the Information Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate to facilitate an agreed resolution of\nmatters at issue in the IC review (for example by using\ntechniques that are used in alternative dispute resolution\nprocesses); and\n(c) allow a person to participate in an IC review by any means of\ncommunication; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "927279a037ec727bb47a405d12d1d2ba478b138e205814d22600b093be478cc9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Procedure in IC review—general",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, for the purposes of an IC\nreview, review an IC reviewable decision by considering the\ndocuments or other material lodged with or provided to the\nInformation Commissioner, and without holding a hearing, if:\n(a) it appears to the Information Commissioner that the issues\nfor determination on the IC review can be adequately\ndetermined in the absence of the review parties; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner is satisfied that there are no\nunusual circumstances that would warrant the Information\nCommissioner holding a hearing; and\n(c) none of the review parties have applied for a hearing under\nsection 55B.\n(2) The Information Commissioner may otherwise:\n(a) conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers\nappropriate; and\n(b) use any technique that the Information Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate to facilitate an agreed resolution of\nmatters at issue in the IC review (for example by using\ntechniques that are used in alternative dispute resolution\nprocesses); and\n(c) allow a person to participate in an IC review by any means of\ncommunication; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55(1) Procedure in IC review—general",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, for the purposes of an IC\nreview, review an IC reviewable decision by considering the\ndocuments or other material lodged with or provided to the\nInformation Commissioner, and without holding a hearing, if:\n(a) it appears to the Information Commissioner that the issues\nfor determination on the IC review can be adequately\ndetermined in the absence of the review parties; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner is satisfied that there are no\nunusual circumstances that would warrant the Information\nCommissioner holding a hearing; and\n(c) none of the review parties have applied for a hearing under\nsection 55B.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, for the purposes of an IC\nreview, review an IC reviewable decision by considering the\ndocuments or other material lodged with or provided to the\nInformation Commissioner, and without holding a hearing, if:\n(a) it appears to the Information Commissioner that the issues\nfor determination on the IC review can be adequately\ndetermined in the absence of the review parties; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner is satisfied that there are no\nunusual circumstances that would warrant the Information\nCommissioner holding a hearing; and\n(c) none of the review parties have applied for a hearing under\nsection 55B.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f5fd5b06f2ee9dcd8ac4451840d6abbc8dfb3b72ba9f31b049ec502da9cbb93",
      "skos:note": "The Information Commissioner may review an IC reviewable decision without holding a hearing under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55(1) Procedure in IC review—general",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, for the purposes of an IC\nreview, review an IC reviewable decision by considering the\ndocuments or other material lodged with or provided to the\nInformation Commissioner, and without holding a hearing, if:\n(a) it appears to the Information Commissioner that the issues\nfor determination on the IC review can be adequately\ndetermined in the absence of the review parties; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner is satisfied that there are no\nunusual circumstances that would warrant the Information\nCommissioner holding a hearing; and\n(c) none of the review parties have applied for a hearing under\nsection 55B."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
