      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55(2) Procedure in IC review—general",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Information Commissioner may otherwise:\n(a) conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers\nappropriate; and\n(b) use any technique that the Information Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate to facilitate an agreed resolution of\nmatters at issue in the IC review (for example by using\ntechniques that are used in alternative dispute resolution\nprocesses); and\n(c) allow a person to participate in an IC review by any means of\ncommunication; and",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Information Commissioner may otherwise:\n(a) conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers\nappropriate; and\n(b) use any technique that the Information Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate to facilitate an agreed resolution of\nmatters at issue in the IC review (for example by using\ntechniques that are used in alternative dispute resolution\nprocesses); and\n(c) allow a person to participate in an IC review by any means of\ncommunication; and",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55-ss-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77b62b4215be2f87862ada1b0d11420e90d15490cb98fd22b080d7310e53bac2",
      "skos:note": "The Information Commissioner may conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers appropriate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55(2) Procedure in IC review—general",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Information Commissioner may otherwise:\n(a) conduct an IC review in whatever way he or she considers\nappropriate; and\n(b) use any technique that the Information Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate to facilitate an agreed resolution of\nmatters at issue in the IC review (for example by using\ntechniques that are used in alternative dispute resolution\nprocesses); and\n(c) allow a person to participate in an IC review by any means of\ncommunication; and"
    },
    {
