    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55A Procedure in IC review—parties to proceeding",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.141",
      "values:originalText": "Who are the review parties?\n(1) The parties to an IC review (the review parties) are as follows:\n(a) the IC review applicant;\n(b) the principal officer of the agency, or the Minister, to whom\nthe request was made;\n(c) an affected third party (if any) required to be notified of the\nIC review application under section 54P (requirement to\nnotify affected third parties);\n(d) a party to the proceeding under subsection (3).\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.\nApplication to become a review party\n(2) If an IC review application is made in relation to an IC reviewable\ndecision, a person whose interests are affected by the IC\nreviewable decision may apply, in writing, to the Information\nCommissioner to be a review party.\n(3) The Information Commissioner may, by notice in writing, make a\nperson who applies under subsection (2) an IC review party.",
      "skos:definition": "Who are the review parties?\n(1) The parties to an IC review (the review parties) are as follows:\n(a) the IC review applicant;\n(b) the principal officer of the agency, or the Minister, to whom\nthe request was made;\n(c) an affected third party (if any) required to be notified of the\nIC review application under section 54P (requirement to\nnotify affected third parties);\n(d) a party to the proceeding under subsection (3).\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.\nApplication to become a review party\n(2) If an IC review application is made in relation to an IC reviewable\ndecision, a person whose interests are affected by the IC\nreviewable decision may apply, in writing, to the Information\nCommissioner to be a review party.\n(3) The Information Commissioner may, by notice in writing, make a\nperson who applies under subsection (2) an IC review party.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7e0d2fc604dfccfcf3dad5c3d6cfff79eeb5cae0e2167ca8a776bf917bdc1757"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55A Procedure in IC review—parties to proceeding",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 141,
      "values:originalText": "Who are the review parties?\n(1) The parties to an IC review (the review parties) are as follows:\n(a) the IC review applicant;\n(b) the principal officer of the agency, or the Minister, to whom\nthe request was made;\n(c) an affected third party (if any) required to be notified of the\nIC review application under section 54P (requirement to\nnotify affected third parties);\n(d) a party to the proceeding under subsection (3).\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.\nApplication to become a review party\n(2) If an IC review application is made in relation to an IC reviewable\ndecision, a person whose interests are affected by the IC\nreviewable decision may apply, in writing, to the Information\nCommissioner to be a review party.\n(3) The Information Commissioner may, by notice in writing, make a\nperson who applies under subsection (2) an IC review party."
    },
