    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55D Procedure in IC review—onus",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.142",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), in an IC review in relation to a request or\nan application under section 48, the agency or Minister concerned\nhas the onus of establishing that:\n(a) a decision given in respect of the request or application is\njustified; or\n(b) the Information Commissioner should give a decision\nadverse to the IC review applicant.\n(2) In an IC review of a decision for which an IC review application is\nmade under section 54M (access grant decisions), the affected third\nparty for the document in relation to which the decision was made\nhas the onus of establishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing the request is justified; or\n(b) the Information Commissioner should give a decision\nadverse to the person who made the request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), in an IC review in relation to a request or\nan application under section 48, the agency or Minister concerned\nhas the onus of establishing that:\n(a) a decision given in respect of the request or application is\njustified; or\n(b) the Information Commissioner should give a decision\nadverse to the IC review applicant.\n(2) In an IC review of a decision for which an IC review application is\nmade under section 54M (access grant decisions), the affected third\nparty for the document in relation to which the decision was made\nhas the onus of establishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing the request is justified; or\n(b) the Information Commissioner should give a decision\nadverse to the person who made the request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "46703b08cdfb550fd240c3b935b8d330871ea8da0da0aaa4d9b9b760839c82fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55D Procedure in IC review—onus",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 142,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), in an IC review in relation to a request or\nan application under section 48, the agency or Minister concerned\nhas the onus of establishing that:\n(a) a decision given in respect of the request or application is\njustified; or\n(b) the Information Commissioner should give a decision\nadverse to the IC review applicant.\n(2) In an IC review of a decision for which an IC review application is\nmade under section 54M (access grant decisions), the affected third\nparty for the document in relation to which the decision was made\nhas the onus of establishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing the request is justified; or\n(b) the Information Commissioner should give a decision\nadverse to the person who made the request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C."
    },
