      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the review parties reach agreement as to the terms of a decision on an IC review"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55G Procedure in IC review—revocation or variation of access",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.144",
      "values:originalText": "refusal decision\n(1) An agency or Minister may vary (or set aside and substitute) an\naccess refusal decision (the original decision) in relation to a\nrequest or an application under section 48 at any time during an IC\nreview of the access refusal decision if the variation or substitution\n(the revised decision) would have an effect of:\n(a) giving access to a document in accordance with the request;\nor\n(b) relieving the IC review applicant from liability to pay a\ncharge; or\n(c) requiring a record of personal information to be amended or\nannotated in accordance with the application.\nNote:\nWhen making the revised decision, a consultation requirement under\nsection 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations\netc.), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal\nprivacy) may apply.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nProcedure in IC review  Division 6\nSection 55H\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(2) If an agency or Minister varies (or sets aside and substitutes) an\naccess refusal decision under subsection (1):\n(a) the agency or Minister must, in writing, notify the\nInformation Commissioner as soon as practicable after the\nagency or Minister makes the variation or substitution; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner must deal with the IC review\napplication for review of the original decision as if it were an\nIC review application for the review of the varied or\nsubstituted decision, subject otherwise to this Part.",
      "skos:definition": "refusal decision\n(1) An agency or Minister may vary (or set aside and substitute) an\naccess refusal decision (the original decision) in relation to a\nrequest or an application under section 48 at any time during an IC\nreview of the access refusal decision if the variation or substitution\n(the revised decision) would have an effect of:\n(a) giving access to a document in accordance with the request;\nor\n(b) relieving the IC review applicant from liability to pay a\ncharge; or\n(c) requiring a record of personal information to be amended or\nannotated in accordance with the application.\nNote:\nWhen making the revised decision, a consultation requirement under\nsection 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations\netc.), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal\nprivacy) may apply.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nProcedure in IC review  Division 6\nSection 55H\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(2) If an agency or Minister varies (or sets aside and substitutes) an\naccess refusal decision under subsection (1):\n(a) the agency or Minister must, in writing, notify the\nInformation Commissioner as soon as practicable after the\nagency or Minister makes the variation or substitution; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner must deal with the IC review\napplication for review of the original decision as if it were an\nIC review application for the review of the varied or\nsubstituted decision, subject otherwise to this Part.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb20867557663d552edf4f62fbe1b46ac60f98e6df0f040540c6e67d17af008e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55G Procedure in IC review—revocation or variation of access",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 144,
      "values:originalText": "refusal decision\n(1) An agency or Minister may vary (or set aside and substitute) an\naccess refusal decision (the original decision) in relation to a\nrequest or an application under section 48 at any time during an IC\nreview of the access refusal decision if the variation or substitution\n(the revised decision) would have an effect of:\n(a) giving access to a document in accordance with the request;\nor\n(b) relieving the IC review applicant from liability to pay a\ncharge; or\n(c) requiring a record of personal information to be amended or\nannotated in accordance with the application.\nNote:\nWhen making the revised decision, a consultation requirement under\nsection 26A (documents affecting Commonwealth-State relations\netc.), 27 (business documents) or 27A (documents affecting personal\nprivacy) may apply.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nProcedure in IC review  Division 6\nSection 55H\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(2) If an agency or Minister varies (or sets aside and substitutes) an\naccess refusal decision under subsection (1):\n(a) the agency or Minister must, in writing, notify the\nInformation Commissioner as soon as practicable after the\nagency or Minister makes the variation or substitution; and\n(b) the Information Commissioner must deal with the IC review\napplication for review of the original decision as if it were an\nIC review application for the review of the varied or\nsubstituted decision, subject otherwise to this Part."
    },
