    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55H(5) Procedure in IC review—reference of questions of law to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.145",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a question of law is referred, the Information Commissioner\nmust not, for the purposes of the IC review:\n(a) give a decision to which the question is relevant before the\nFederal Court of Australia makes a decision in relation to the\nreference; or\n(b) proceed in a manner, or make a decision, that is inconsistent\nwith the opinion of the Federal Court of Australia on the\nquestion.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a question of law is referred, the Information Commissioner\nmust not, for the purposes of the IC review:\n(a) give a decision to which the question is relevant before the\nFederal Court of Australia makes a decision in relation to the\nreference; or\n(b) proceed in a manner, or make a decision, that is inconsistent\nwith the opinion of the Federal Court of Australia on the\nquestion.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5-norm"
        },
