          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5-logic-argumentation-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "900b02026cf34c3e84f8564b7a5e14ef66ad691087616a926f9c44d95e553d29",
      "skos:note": "Must not give a decision before Federal Court of Australia makes a decision on the question."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55H(5) Procedure in IC review—reference of questions of law to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 145,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a question of law is referred, the Information Commissioner\nmust not, for the purposes of the IC review:\n(a) give a decision to which the question is relevant before the\nFederal Court of Australia makes a decision in relation to the\nreference; or\n(b) proceed in a manner, or make a decision, that is inconsistent\nwith the opinion of the Federal Court of Australia on the\nquestion."
    },
