      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "disclosure of documents by, the Federal Court of\nAustralia\nIf a question of law is referred under section 55H:\n(a) the Information Commissioner must cause all documents and\ninformation in the possession of the Information\nCommissioner that relate to the IC review and to the\nreference to be sent to the Federal Court of Australia; and\n(b) at the conclusion of the proceeding before the Federal Court\nof Australia, the Court must cause the documents to be\nreturned to the Information Commissioner.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nDecision on IC review  Division 7\nSection 55K\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "disclosure of documents by, the Federal Court of\nAustralia\nIf a question of law is referred under section 55H:\n(a) the Information Commissioner must cause all documents and\ninformation in the possession of the Information\nCommissioner that relate to the IC review and to the\nreference to be sent to the Federal Court of Australia; and\n(b) at the conclusion of the proceeding before the Federal Court\nof Australia, the Court must cause the documents to be\nreturned to the Information Commissioner.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nDecision on IC review  Division 7\nSection 55K\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55j-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55j-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "82dd27344ba983def7d7f23f5516b08c95fd1deea1bbab6f1ffbe4d28a6128a1",
      "skos:note": "Must send documents to Federal Court of Australia upon request."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55J Procedure in IC review—sending of documents to, and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "disclosure of documents by, the Federal Court of\nAustralia\nIf a question of law is referred under section 55H:\n(a) the Information Commissioner must cause all documents and\ninformation in the possession of the Information\nCommissioner that relate to the IC review and to the\nreference to be sent to the Federal Court of Australia; and\n(b) at the conclusion of the proceeding before the Federal Court\nof Australia, the Court must cause the documents to be\nreturned to the Information Commissioner.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nDecision on IC review  Division 7\nSection 55K\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55j-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
