    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55K Decision on IC review—decision of Information Commissioner",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.147",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust make a decision in writing:\n(a) affirming the IC reviewable decision; or\n(b) varying the IC reviewable decision; or\n(c) setting aside the IC reviewable decision and making a\ndecision in substitution for that decision.\n(2) For the purposes of implementing a decision on an IC review, the\nInformation Commissioner may perform the functions, and\nexercise the powers, of the person who made the IC reviewable\ndecision.\n(3) A decision of the Information Commissioner on an IC review has\nthe same effect as a decision of the agency or Minister who made\nthe IC reviewable decision.\nContent of the decision\n(4) A decision on an IC review must include the following:\n(a) a statement of reasons for the decision;\n(b) a statement of the rights of the review parties to apply to the\nTribunal for review of the decision under section 57A.\n(5) However, a decision on an IC review must not include:\n(a) information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1); or\n(b) exempt matter.\nNote:\nSubsection 25(1) deals with information about the existence or\notherwise of certain documents.\nProviding copy of decision\n(6) The Information Commissioner must give a copy of a decision on\nan IC review to each review party.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust make a decision in writing:\n(a) affirming the IC reviewable decision; or\n(b) varying the IC reviewable decision; or\n(c) setting aside the IC reviewable decision and making a\ndecision in substitution for that decision.\n(2) For the purposes of implementing a decision on an IC review, the\nInformation Commissioner may perform the functions, and\nexercise the powers, of the person who made the IC reviewable\ndecision.\n(3) A decision of the Information Commissioner on an IC review has\nthe same effect as a decision of the agency or Minister who made\nthe IC reviewable decision.\nContent of the decision\n(4) A decision on an IC review must include the following:\n(a) a statement of reasons for the decision;\n(b) a statement of the rights of the review parties to apply to the\nTribunal for review of the decision under section 57A.\n(5) However, a decision on an IC review must not include:\n(a) information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1); or\n(b) exempt matter.\nNote:\nSubsection 25(1) deals with information about the existence or\notherwise of certain documents.\nProviding copy of decision\n(6) The Information Commissioner must give a copy of a decision on\nan IC review to each review party.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55k-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b607da8a40a122373c96acfe58674bd048b140cdc51a51f87b383519d25f3650"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55K Decision on IC review—decision of Information Commissioner",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 147,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After undertaking an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust make a decision in writing:\n(a) affirming the IC reviewable decision; or\n(b) varying the IC reviewable decision; or\n(c) setting aside the IC reviewable decision and making a\ndecision in substitution for that decision.\n(2) For the purposes of implementing a decision on an IC review, the\nInformation Commissioner may perform the functions, and\nexercise the powers, of the person who made the IC reviewable\ndecision.\n(3) A decision of the Information Commissioner on an IC review has\nthe same effect as a decision of the agency or Minister who made\nthe IC reviewable decision.\nContent of the decision\n(4) A decision on an IC review must include the following:\n(a) a statement of reasons for the decision;\n(b) a statement of the rights of the review parties to apply to the\nTribunal for review of the decision under section 57A.\n(5) However, a decision on an IC review must not include:\n(a) information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1); or\n(b) exempt matter.\nNote:\nSubsection 25(1) deals with information about the existence or\notherwise of certain documents.\nProviding copy of decision\n(6) The Information Commissioner must give a copy of a decision on\nan IC review to each review party."
    },
