      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, in a decision under\nsection 55K, make a decision that requires, or has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record that relates to a\nrecord of an opinion only if he or she is satisfied of either (or both)\nof the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must not, in a decision under\nsection 55K, make a decision that requires, or has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if he or she is\nsatisfied of either of the following:\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nDecision on IC review  Division 7\nSection 55N\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, in a decision under\nsection 55K, make a decision that requires, or has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record that relates to a\nrecord of an opinion only if he or she is satisfied of either (or both)\nof the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must not, in a decision under\nsection 55K, make a decision that requires, or has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if he or she is\nsatisfied of either of the following:\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nDecision on IC review  Division 7\nSection 55N\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55m-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "572f440856668fc6f164298c5688457ecc943240faf7a1b54b1966ebaa545130"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55M Decision on IC review—limitation on amending records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 148,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may, in a decision under\nsection 55K, make a decision that requires, or has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record that relates to a\nrecord of an opinion only if he or she is satisfied of either (or both)\nof the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must not, in a decision under\nsection 55K, make a decision that requires, or has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if he or she is\nsatisfied of either of the following:\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nDecision on IC review  Division 7\nSection 55N\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal."
    },
