    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55Q Decision on IC review—correction of errors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error in a\ndecision under section 55K of the Information Commissioner on an\nIC review.\nExample:\nThe following are examples of obvious errors:\n(a)\nan obvious clerical or typographical error in the text of the\ndecision or statement of reasons;\n(b)\nan inconsistency between the decision and the statement of\nreasons.\n(2) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error:\n(a) on an application by a review party; or\n(b) on the Information Commissioner’s initiative.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nInformation gathering powers  Division 8\nSection 55R\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error in a\ndecision under section 55K of the Information Commissioner on an\nIC review.\nExample:\nThe following are examples of obvious errors:\n(a)\nan obvious clerical or typographical error in the text of the\ndecision or statement of reasons;\n(b)\nan inconsistency between the decision and the statement of\nreasons.\n(2) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error:\n(a) on an application by a review party; or\n(b) on the Information Commissioner’s initiative.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nInformation gathering powers  Division 8\nSection 55R\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55q-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ec07180150e5118f21f6dbdabe5be450a23fb20ac3240c8a636f93c13799d1dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55Q Decision on IC review—correction of errors",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error in a\ndecision under section 55K of the Information Commissioner on an\nIC review.\nExample:\nThe following are examples of obvious errors:\n(a)\nan obvious clerical or typographical error in the text of the\ndecision or statement of reasons;\n(b)\nan inconsistency between the decision and the statement of\nreasons.\n(2) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error:\n(a) on an application by a review party; or\n(b) on the Information Commissioner’s initiative.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nInformation gathering powers  Division 8\nSection 55R\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
