    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55S Information gathering powers—dealings with documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "What the Information Commissioner may do with documents\n(1) The Information Commissioner may do any of the following in\nrelation to any documents produced in accordance with a notice\nunder subsection 55R(3):\n(a) take possession of the documents;\n(b) make copies of the documents;\n(c) take extracts from the documents;\n(d) hold the documents for a period that is necessary for the\npurposes of the IC review.\nInformation Commissioner must permit access by those entitled\n(2) For the purposes of an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust permit a person to inspect a document that the person would\nbe entitled to inspect if the document were not held by the\nInformation Commissioner.\n(3) The Information Commissioner must permit the person to inspect\nthe document at any reasonable time.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nInformation gathering powers  Division 8\nSection 55T\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "What the Information Commissioner may do with documents\n(1) The Information Commissioner may do any of the following in\nrelation to any documents produced in accordance with a notice\nunder subsection 55R(3):\n(a) take possession of the documents;\n(b) make copies of the documents;\n(c) take extracts from the documents;\n(d) hold the documents for a period that is necessary for the\npurposes of the IC review.\nInformation Commissioner must permit access by those entitled\n(2) For the purposes of an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust permit a person to inspect a document that the person would\nbe entitled to inspect if the document were not held by the\nInformation Commissioner.\n(3) The Information Commissioner must permit the person to inspect\nthe document at any reasonable time.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nInformation gathering powers  Division 8\nSection 55T\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55s-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55s-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26b7972b0eda4dc96ca8d4d4d8c268704052728e9457bf5c81fbe7df5c9df57f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55S Information gathering powers—dealings with documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "What the Information Commissioner may do with documents\n(1) The Information Commissioner may do any of the following in\nrelation to any documents produced in accordance with a notice\nunder subsection 55R(3):\n(a) take possession of the documents;\n(b) make copies of the documents;\n(c) take extracts from the documents;\n(d) hold the documents for a period that is necessary for the\npurposes of the IC review.\nInformation Commissioner must permit access by those entitled\n(2) For the purposes of an IC review, the Information Commissioner\nmust permit a person to inspect a document that the person would\nbe entitled to inspect if the document were not held by the\nInformation Commissioner.\n(3) The Information Commissioner must permit the person to inspect\nthe document at any reasonable time.\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nInformation gathering powers  Division 8\nSection 55T\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
