    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55w",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55W Information gathering powers—obliging persons to appear",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55w"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "Notice to appear\n(1) The Information Commissioner may, by written notice, require a\nperson to appear before the Information Commissioner to answer\nquestions for the purposes of an IC review.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) state that the person must comply with the notice at a\nspecified time that is not less than 14 days after the time at\nwhich the person is given the notice; and\n(c) specify the place at which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nOffence for failure to comply\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (1); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.",
      "skos:definition": "Notice to appear\n(1) The Information Commissioner may, by written notice, require a\nperson to appear before the Information Commissioner to answer\nquestions for the purposes of an IC review.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) state that the person must comply with the notice at a\nspecified time that is not less than 14 days after the time at\nwhich the person is given the notice; and\n(c) specify the place at which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nOffence for failure to comply\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (1); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55w-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55w-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55w-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b180a071b43029061c1cf8546036bfae2371bf3dfd6536904222a87f13e4746a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55w",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55W Information gathering powers—obliging persons to appear",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "Notice to appear\n(1) The Information Commissioner may, by written notice, require a\nperson to appear before the Information Commissioner to answer\nquestions for the purposes of an IC review.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) state that the person must comply with the notice at a\nspecified time that is not less than 14 days after the time at\nwhich the person is given the notice; and\n(c) specify the place at which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nOffence for failure to comply\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (1); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement."
    },
