    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55X Information gathering powers—administration of oath or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55x"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "affirmation\n(1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information\nCommissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the\nInformation Commissioner may:\n(a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and\n(b) examine the person on oath or affirmation.\n(2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the\npurposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers\nthe person will give will be true.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is required under this section to be examined on\noath or affirmation; and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\n6 months\nimprisonment.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.",
      "skos:definition": "affirmation\n(1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information\nCommissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the\nInformation Commissioner may:\n(a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and\n(b) examine the person on oath or affirmation.\n(2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the\npurposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers\nthe person will give will be true.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is required under this section to be examined on\noath or affirmation; and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\n6 months\nimprisonment.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a69ad33c292fe18441e94306be54fc9a52e27fb2686932199c0b719fa2d803b2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55x",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55X Information gathering powers—administration of oath or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "affirmation\n(1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information\nCommissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the\nInformation Commissioner may:\n(a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and\n(b) examine the person on oath or affirmation.\n(2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the\npurposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers\nthe person will give will be true.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is required under this section to be examined on\noath or affirmation; and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\n6 months\nimprisonment.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-1",
