    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55za",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55ZA Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55za"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "scope\nThis Division applies in an IC review of a decision in relation to a\ndocument that:\n(a) is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33\n(national security documents); and\n(b) relates directly or indirectly to:\n(i) the performance of the functions or duties, or the\nexercise of the powers, of a body mentioned in\nparagraph (a) of the definition of intelligence agency in\nsubsection 3(1) of the Inspector-General of Intelligence\nand Security Act 1986; or\n(ii) the performance of an intelligence function (within the\nmeaning of that Act) of a body mentioned in\nparagraph (b) of that definition; and\n(c) is not a document of the Inspector-General of Intelligence\nand Security.",
      "skos:definition": "scope\nThis Division applies in an IC review of a decision in relation to a\ndocument that:\n(a) is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33\n(national security documents); and\n(b) relates directly or indirectly to:\n(i) the performance of the functions or duties, or the\nexercise of the powers, of a body mentioned in\nparagraph (a) of the definition of intelligence agency in\nsubsection 3(1) of the Inspector-General of Intelligence\nand Security Act 1986; or\n(ii) the performance of an intelligence function (within the\nmeaning of that Act) of a body mentioned in\nparagraph (b) of that definition; and\n(c) is not a document of the Inspector-General of Intelligence\nand Security.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55za-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "23bfb531937233730d04bc96d205526de7999848533ce370c4c14990ef3769a4",
      "skos:note": "Scope of Division"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55za",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55ZA Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "scope\nThis Division applies in an IC review of a decision in relation to a\ndocument that:\n(a) is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33\n(national security documents); and\n(b) relates directly or indirectly to:\n(i) the performance of the functions or duties, or the\nexercise of the powers, of a body mentioned in\nparagraph (a) of the definition of intelligence agency in\nsubsection 3(1) of the Inspector-General of Intelligence\nand Security Act 1986; or\n(ii) the performance of an intelligence function (within the\nmeaning of that Act) of a body mentioned in\nparagraph (b) of that definition; and\n(c) is not a document of the Inspector-General of Intelligence\nand Security."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55za-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55za"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55ZB Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55zb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "request to give evidence\n(1) Before determining that a document is not an exempt document\nunder section 33, the Information Commissioner must request the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally\nand give evidence on:\n(a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to,\nbe caused to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nEvidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security  Division 9\nSection 55ZB\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nif access to the document were given in accordance with the\nrequest; or\n(b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with\nthe request would divulge any information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n(2) Before determining that an agency or Minister must grant access to\na copy of the document with deletions, the Information\nCommissioner must request the Inspector-General to appear\npersonally and give evidence on:\n(a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to,\nbe caused to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;\nif the proposed deletions were not made; or\n(b) whether giving access to the document without the proposed\ndeletions would divulge any information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n(3) Before hearing the evidence of the Inspector-General, the\nInformation Commissioner must hear any evidence to be given or\nsubmissions to be made by, or on behalf of, the agency to which, or\nthe Minister to whom, the request was made for access to the\ndocument.",
      "skos:definition": "request to give evidence\n(1) Before determining that a document is not an exempt document\nunder section 33, the Information Commissioner must request the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally\nand give evidence on:\n(a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to,\nbe caused to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nEvidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security  Division 9\nSection 55ZB\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nif access to the document were given in accordance with the\nrequest; or\n(b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with\nthe request would divulge any information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n(2) Before determining that an agency or Minister must grant access to\na copy of the document with deletions, the Information\nCommissioner must request the Inspector-General to appear\npersonally and give evidence on:\n(a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to,\nbe caused to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;\nif the proposed deletions were not made; or\n(b) whether giving access to the document without the proposed\ndeletions would divulge any information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the commu",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c3db9088f81a1bb67fa593649bc0bc85f9f0abc5eb84ec14b86d5290f50dc22a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55zb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55ZB Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "request to give evidence\n(1) Before determining that a document is not an exempt document\nunder section 33, the Information Commissioner must request the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally\nand give evidence on:\n(a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to,\nbe caused to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nEvidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security  Division 9\nSection 55ZB\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nif access to the document were given in accordance with the\nrequest; or\n(b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with\nthe request would divulge any information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n(2) Before determining that an agency or Minister must grant access to\na copy of the document with deletions, the Information\nCommissioner must request the Inspector-General to appear\npersonally and give evidence on:\n(a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to,\nbe caused to:\n(i) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;\nif the proposed deletions were not made; or\n(b) whether giving access to the document without the proposed\ndeletions would divulge any information or matter\ncommunicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign\ngovernment, an authority of a foreign government or an\ninternational organisation to the Government of the\nCommonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a\nperson receiving the communication on behalf of the\nCommonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.\n(3) Before hearing the evidence of the Inspector-General, the\nInformation Commissioner must hear any evidence to be given or\nsubmissions to be made by, or on behalf of, the agency to which, or\nthe Minister to whom, the request was made for access to the\ndocument."
    },
