    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55ZC Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55zc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "compliance with request\nThe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must comply\nwith a request under section 55ZB unless, in the opinion of the\nInspector-General, the Inspector-General is not appropriately\nqualified to give evidence on the matters in relation to which the\nInspector-General has been requested to give evidence.",
      "skos:definition": "compliance with request\nThe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must comply\nwith a request under section 55ZB unless, in the opinion of the\nInspector-General, the Inspector-General is not appropriately\nqualified to give evidence on the matters in relation to which the\nInspector-General has been requested to give evidence.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zc-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "769bdede4160038fa677e5c5a1219a420b1031b01b1176f8a4369f6c77ebe5f3",
      "skos:note": "Must comply with request unless not qualified to give evidence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55zc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55ZC Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "compliance with request\nThe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must comply\nwith a request under section 55ZB unless, in the opinion of the\nInspector-General, the Inspector-General is not appropriately\nqualified to give evidence on the matters in relation to which the\nInspector-General has been requested to give evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zc-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zc"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zc-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55ZD Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-55zd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "procedural matters\n(1) This section applies for the purposes of enabling the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security to comply with a\nrequest under section 55ZB.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must allow the Inspector-General\nto take possession of, and make copies of or take extracts from, any\ndocument given to the Information Commissioner for the purposes\nof the proceeding.\n(3) The Inspector-General may require the production of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the document that is claimed to be an exempt document\nunder section 33 by the agency to which or the Minister to\nwhom the request was made for access to the document;\n(b) any document of an agency or official document of a\nMinister that relates to the document mentioned in\nsubsection (2) by the agency or Minister.\n(4) The Inspector-General may make copies of, or take extracts from,\nthe documents mentioned in subsection (3).\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nEvidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security  Division 9\nSection 55ZD\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(5) After the period that is reasonably necessary for the purposes of\ngiving evidence to the Information Commissioner, the\nInspector-General must:\n(a) return the original of any document to the Information\nCommissioner or to the agency or Minister; and\n(b) destroy any copies of or extracts taken from any document.\n(6) The Inspector-General must permit a person to inspect a document\nthat the person would be entitled to inspect if the document were\nnot held by the Inspector-General.\n(7) The Inspector-General must permit the person to inspect the\ndocument at all reasonable times.\n(8) The Information Commissioner must allow the Inspector-General a\nperiod within which to consider the documents mentioned in\nsubsections (2) to (4) that is reasonable having regard to:\n(a) the nature of the evidence that the Inspector-General has been\nrequested to give; and\n(b) the time required by the Inspector-General to perform the\nInspector-General’s other functions.",
      "skos:definition": "procedural matters\n(1) This section applies for the purposes of enabling the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security to comply with a\nrequest under section 55ZB.\n(2) The Information Commissioner must allow the Inspector-General\nto take possession of, and make copies of or take extracts from, any\ndocument given to the Information Commissioner for the purposes\nof the proceeding.\n(3) The Inspector-General may require the production of the\nfollowing:\n(a) the document that is claimed to be an exempt document\nunder section 33 by the agency to which or the Minister to\nwhom the request was made for access to the document;\n(b) any document of an agency or official document of a\nMinister that relates to the document mentioned in\nsubsection (2) by the agency or Minister.\n(4) The Inspector-General may make copies of, or take extracts from,\nthe documents mentioned in subsection (3).\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nEvidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security  Division 9\nSection 55ZD\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(5) After the period that is reasonably necessary for the purposes of\ngiving evidence to the Information Commissioner, the\nInspector-General must:\n(a) return the original of any document to the Information\nCommissioner or to the agency or Minister; and\n(b) destroy any copies of or extracts taken from any document.\n(6) The Inspector-General must permit a person to inspect a document\nthat the person would be entitled to inspect if the document were\nnot held by the Inspector-General.\n(7) The Inspector-General must permit the person to inspect the\ndocument at all reasonable times.\n(8) The Information Commissioner must allow the Inspector-General a\nperiod within which to consider the documents mentioned in\nsubsections (2) to (4) that is reasonable having regard to:\n(a) the nature of the evidence that the Inspector-General has been\nrequested to give; and\n(b) the time required by the Inspector-General to perform",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zd-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zd-ss-4"
        },
