    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56(6) Appeals—appeals to Federal Court of Australia on questions of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-56-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.162",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Without limiting subsection (5), the orders that the Federal Court\nof Australia may make include the following:\n(a) an order affirming the decision of the Information\nCommissioner;\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nAppeals  Division 10\nSection 56A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(b) an order setting aside the decision of the Information\nCommissioner and making a decision in substitution for the\ndecision;\n(c) an order remitting the case to be considered and decided\nagain by the Information Commissioner in accordance with\nthe directions of the Court:\n(i) with or without the holding of a hearing; and\n(ii) with or without the hearing of further evidence.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Without limiting subsection (5), the orders that the Federal Court\nof Australia may make include the following:\n(a) an order affirming the decision of the Information\nCommissioner;\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nAppeals  Division 10\nSection 56A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(b) an order setting aside the decision of the Information\nCommissioner and making a decision in substitution for the\ndecision;\n(c) an order remitting the case to be considered and decided\nagain by the Information Commissioner in accordance with\nthe directions of the Court:\n(i) with or without the holding of a hearing; and\n(ii) with or without the hearing of further evidence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd63d8fa8bc7ede887d3867b7cff31cbb5b8a1d843d075934e5b4b1cc2fd739d",
      "skos:note": "The Federal Court of Australia may not make certain decisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-56-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56(6) Appeals—appeals to Federal Court of Australia on questions of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 162,
      "values:originalText": "(6) Without limiting subsection (5), the orders that the Federal Court\nof Australia may make include the following:\n(a) an order affirming the decision of the Information\nCommissioner;\n\n\nReview by Information Commissioner  Part VII\nAppeals  Division 10\nSection 56A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(b) an order setting aside the decision of the Information\nCommissioner and making a decision in substitution for the\ndecision;\n(c) an order remitting the case to be considered and decided\nagain by the Information Commissioner in accordance with\nthe directions of the Court:\n(i) with or without the holding of a hearing; and\n(ii) with or without the hearing of further evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
