    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56A Appeals—Federal Court of Australia may make findings of fact",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-56a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a review party appeals to the Federal Court of Australia under\nsection 56, the Court may make findings of fact if:\n(a) the findings of fact are not inconsistent with findings of fact\nmade by the Information Commissioner (other than findings\nmade by the Information Commissioner as the result of an\nerror of law); and\n(b) it appears to the Court that it is convenient for the Court to\nmake the findings of fact, having regard to all of the\nfollowing:\n(i) the extent (if any) to which it is necessary for facts to be\nfound;\n(ii) the means by which those facts might be established;\n(iii) the expeditious and efficient resolution of the whole of\nthe matter to which the IC review relates;\n(iv) the relative expense to the parties of the Court, rather\nthan the Information Commissioner, making the\nfindings of fact;\n(v) the relative delay to the parties of the Court, rather than\nthe Information Commissioner, making the findings of\nfact;\n(vi) whether any of the parties considers that it is\nappropriate for the Court, rather than the Information\nCommissioner, to make the findings of fact;\n(vii) such other matters (if any) as the Court considers\nrelevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a review party appeals to the Federal Court of Australia under\nsection 56, the Court may make findings of fact if:\n(a) the findings of fact are not inconsistent with findings of fact\nmade by the Information Commissioner (other than findings\nmade by the Information Commissioner as the result of an\nerror of law); and\n(b) it appears to the Court that it is convenient for the Court to\nmake the findings of fact, having regard to all of the\nfollowing:\n(i) the extent (if any) to which it is necessary for facts to be\nfound;\n(ii) the means by which those facts might be established;\n(iii) the expeditious and efficient resolution of the whole of\nthe matter to which the IC review relates;\n(iv) the relative expense to the parties of the Court, rather\nthan the Information Commissioner, making the\nfindings of fact;\n(v) the relative delay to the parties of the Court, rather than\nthe Information Commissioner, making the findings of\nfact;\n(vi) whether any of the parties considers that it is\nappropriate for the Court, rather than the Information\nCommissioner, to make the findings of fact;\n(vii) such other matters (if any) as the Court considers\nrelevant.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-56a-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78871a730ae160cd08330f6f4a2d2fac660dadb8ff271419aa70625f022bbbd8",
      "skos:note": "The Federal Court of Australia may make findings of fact in certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-56a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56A Appeals—Federal Court of Australia may make findings of fact",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 163,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a review party appeals to the Federal Court of Australia under\nsection 56, the Court may make findings of fact if:\n(a) the findings of fact are not inconsistent with findings of fact\nmade by the Information Commissioner (other than findings\nmade by the Information Commissioner as the result of an\nerror of law); and\n(b) it appears to the Court that it is convenient for the Court to\nmake the findings of fact, having regard to all of the\nfollowing:\n(i) the extent (if any) to which it is necessary for facts to be\nfound;\n(ii) the means by which those facts might be established;\n(iii) the expeditious and efficient resolution of the whole of\nthe matter to which the IC review relates;\n(iv) the relative expense to the parties of the Court, rather\nthan the Information Commissioner, making the\nfindings of fact;\n(v) the relative delay to the parties of the Court, rather than\nthe Information Commissioner, making the findings of\nfact;\n(vi) whether any of the parties considers that it is\nappropriate for the Court, rather than the Information\nCommissioner, to make the findings of fact;\n(vii) such other matters (if any) as the Court considers\nrelevant."
    },
