    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-57a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57A(1) Tribunal reviewable decisions—which decisions are",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 166,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application may be made to the Tribunal for review of the\nfollowing decisions:\n(a) a decision of the Information Commissioner under\nsection 55K on an IC review;\n(b) if the Information Commissioner makes a decision under\nparagraph 54W(b) (matters inappropriate for IC review)—the\nIC reviewable decision in relation to which the Information\nCommissioner makes the decision.\nNote 1:\nAn application for the review of a decision may be made by a person\nwhose interests are affected by the decision (see section 17 of the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal Act 2024).\nNote 2:\nFor the time period for making an application, see sections 18 to 20 of\nthe Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024.\nTime for applying to Tribunal if Information Commissioner\ndeclines to review decision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "May apply for review",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Person whose interests are affected",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Application may be made"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57A(2) Tribunal reviewable decisions—which decisions are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-57a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.166",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Despite section 18 of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024\nan application for review of an IC reviewable decision mentioned\nin paragraph (1)(b) of this section must be made within the period:\n(a) starting on the day on which the decision by the Information\nCommissioner under paragraph 54W(b) of this Act is made;\nand\n(b) ending at the end of the period prescribed for the purposes of\nsubsection 18(1) of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act\n2024.\nNo referral to guidance and appeals panel",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Despite section 18 of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024\nan application for review of an IC reviewable decision mentioned\nin paragraph (1)(b) of this section must be made within the period:\n(a) starting on the day on which the decision by the Information\nCommissioner under paragraph 54W(b) of this Act is made;\nand\n(b) ending at the end of the period prescribed for the purposes of\nsubsection 18(1) of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act\n2024.\nNo referral to guidance and appeals panel",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-57a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "acd897021654f7d038a20531e5b7d5cb9913c348e1bba38be23eca6578307912",
      "skos:note": "Application for review of IC reviewable decision must be made within a specified period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-57a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57A(2) Tribunal reviewable decisions—which decisions are",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 166,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Despite section 18 of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024\nan application for review of an IC reviewable decision mentioned\nin paragraph (1)(b) of this section must be made within the period:\n(a) starting on the day on which the decision by the Information\nCommissioner under paragraph 54W(b) of this Act is made;\nand\n(b) ending at the end of the period prescribed for the purposes of\nsubsection 18(1) of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act\n2024.\nNo referral to guidance and appeals panel"
    },
    {
