    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58 Powers of Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-58"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, in proceedings under this Part, the Tribunal\nhas power, in addition to any other power, to review any decision\nthat has been made by an agency or Minister in respect of the\nrequest and to decide any matter in relation to the request that,\nunder this Act, could have been or could be decided by an agency\nor Minister, and any decision of the Tribunal under this section has\nthe same effect as a decision of the agency or Minister.\n(2) Where, in proceedings under this Act, it is established that a\ndocument is an exempt document, the Tribunal does not have\npower to decide that access to the document, so far as it contains\nexempt matter, is to be granted.\n(6) The powers of the Tribunal under this section extend to matters\nrelating to charges payable under this Act in relation to a request.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to this section, in proceedings under this Part, the Tribunal\nhas power, in addition to any other power, to review any decision\nthat has been made by an agency or Minister in respect of the\nrequest and to decide any matter in relation to the request that,\nunder this Act, could have been or could be decided by an agency\nor Minister, and any decision of the Tribunal under this section has\nthe same effect as a decision of the agency or Minister.\n(2) Where, in proceedings under this Act, it is established that a\ndocument is an exempt document, the Tribunal does not have\npower to decide that access to the document, so far as it contains\nexempt matter, is to be granted.\n(6) The powers of the Tribunal under this section extend to matters\nrelating to charges payable under this Act in relation to a request.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "deb380e5c23964544de2144010a155bd9fb51835e21a387e6f5352f20b43e5ec"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-58",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58 Powers of Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, in proceedings under this Part, the Tribunal\nhas power, in addition to any other power, to review any decision\nthat has been made by an agency or Minister in respect of the\nrequest and to decide any matter in relation to the request that,\nunder this Act, could have been or could be decided by an agency\nor Minister, and any decision of the Tribunal under this section has\nthe same effect as a decision of the agency or Minister.\n(2) Where, in proceedings under this Act, it is established that a\ndocument is an exempt document, the Tribunal does not have\npower to decide that access to the document, so far as it contains\nexempt matter, is to be granted.\n(6) The powers of the Tribunal under this section extend to matters\nrelating to charges payable under this Act in relation to a request."
    },
    {
