    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58AA Powers of Tribunal—limitation on amending records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-58aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Tribunal may, in a decision on an application to the Tribunal\nunder section 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the\neffect of requiring, that an amendment be made to a record that\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nPowers of Tribunal  Division 3\nSection 58AA\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nrelates to a record of an opinion only if the Tribunal is satisfied of\neither (or both) of the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion.\n(2) The Tribunal must not, in a decision on an application under\nsection 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if it is satisfied\nof either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Tribunal may, in a decision on an application to the Tribunal\nunder section 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the\neffect of requiring, that an amendment be made to a record that\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nPowers of Tribunal  Division 3\nSection 58AA\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nrelates to a record of an opinion only if the Tribunal is satisfied of\neither (or both) of the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion.\n(2) The Tribunal must not, in a decision on an application under\nsection 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if it is satisfied\nof either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bfe8b9c037f6213d6ac1614fc8d930bdc591fa790b7bf96596d14c01621779c5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-58aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AA Powers of Tribunal—limitation on amending records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Tribunal may, in a decision on an application to the Tribunal\nunder section 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the\neffect of requiring, that an amendment be made to a record that\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nPowers of Tribunal  Division 3\nSection 58AA\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nrelates to a record of an opinion only if the Tribunal is satisfied of\neither (or both) of the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion.\n(2) The Tribunal must not, in a decision on an application under\nsection 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if it is satisfied\nof either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal."
    },
    {
