        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "91e0ea544c9fe29c0ad9fd69409f809571e71f5ceeee9fab3aeda55dc4f31b0d",
      "skos:note": "The Tribunal may require an amendment to a record of an opinion if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AA(1) Powers of Tribunal—limitation on amending records",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Tribunal may, in a decision on an application to the Tribunal\nunder section 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the\neffect of requiring, that an amendment be made to a record that\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nPowers of Tribunal  Division 3\nSection 58AA\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\nrelates to a record of an opinion only if the Tribunal is satisfied of\neither (or both) of the following:\n(a) the opinion was based on a mistake of fact;\n(b) the author of the opinion was biased, unqualified to form the\nopinion or acted improperly in conducting the factual\ninquiries that led to the formation of the opinion."
    },
