      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Tribunal must not, in a decision on an application under\nsection 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if it is satisfied\nof either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Tribunal must not, in a decision on an application under\nsection 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if it is satisfied\nof either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0d8ada615847c47c1f47f796d7ab67753991f758aeb5dcb70c159d2b7da59d4b",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal cannot amend records under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-58aa-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58AA(2) Powers of Tribunal—limitation on amending records",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Tribunal must not, in a decision on an application under\nsection 57A, make a decision that requires, or that has the effect of\nrequiring, that an amendment be made to a record if it is satisfied\nof either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves the\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal."
    },
    {
