    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-60aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60AA Procedure in Tribunal—requirement to notify affected third",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-60aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.171",
      "values:originalText": "parties\nScope\n(1) This section applies if an application is made to the Tribunal under\nsection 57A for the review of a decision not to give access to a\ndocument to which a consultation requirement applies under\nsection 26A, 27 or 27A (whether the decision is made by the\nInformation Commissioner, an agency or a Minister).\nRequirement to notify\n(2) The agency to which, or the Minister to whom, the request was\nmade for access to the document must, as soon as practicable, take\nall reasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the\ndocument of the application to the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "parties\nScope\n(1) This section applies if an application is made to the Tribunal under\nsection 57A for the review of a decision not to give access to a\ndocument to which a consultation requirement applies under\nsection 26A, 27 or 27A (whether the decision is made by the\nInformation Commissioner, an agency or a Minister).\nRequirement to notify\n(2) The agency to which, or the Minister to whom, the request was\nmade for access to the document must, as soon as practicable, take\nall reasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the\ndocument of the application to the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-60aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-60aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3e77857035d342cc37b8700be499cb2a22516a626e6ea7fe72c995ed6d6f8248"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-60aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60AA Procedure in Tribunal—requirement to notify affected third",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 171,
      "values:originalText": "parties\nScope\n(1) This section applies if an application is made to the Tribunal under\nsection 57A for the review of a decision not to give access to a\ndocument to which a consultation requirement applies under\nsection 26A, 27 or 27A (whether the decision is made by the\nInformation Commissioner, an agency or a Minister).\nRequirement to notify\n(2) The agency to which, or the Minister to whom, the request was\nmade for access to the document must, as soon as practicable, take\nall reasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the\ndocument of the application to the Tribunal."
    },
