    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61 Onus",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-61"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In proceedings under this Part for review of a decision in relation\nto a request, or in relation to an application under section 48\n(a personal records application):\n(a) if an agency or a Minister applied for the review—the agency\nor Minister has the onus of establishing that the decision is\nnot justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision\nadverse to the applicant in relation to the request or the\npersonal records application; or\n(b) if the applicant in relation to the request or the personal\nrecords application applied for the review—the agency to\nwhich, or the Minister to whom, the request or personal\nrecords application was made has the onus of establishing\nthat the decision is justified, or that the Tribunal should give\na decision adverse to the applicant.\n(2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to\ngive access to a document to which a consultation requirement\napplies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for\nthe document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the\naffected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of\nestablishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is\njustified; or\n(b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person\nwho made the relevant request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In proceedings under this Part for review of a decision in relation\nto a request, or in relation to an application under section 48\n(a personal records application):\n(a) if an agency or a Minister applied for the review—the agency\nor Minister has the onus of establishing that the decision is\nnot justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision\nadverse to the applicant in relation to the request or the\npersonal records application; or\n(b) if the applicant in relation to the request or the personal\nrecords application applied for the review—the agency to\nwhich, or the Minister to whom, the request or personal\nrecords application was made has the onus of establishing\nthat the decision is justified, or that the Tribunal should give\na decision adverse to the applicant.\n(2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to\ngive access to a document to which a consultation requirement\napplies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for\nthe document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the\naffected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of\nestablishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is\njustified; or\n(b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person\nwho made the relevant request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c0069c1b0e0e91068478f73632789ecef3d945cadc5000395493e46962e666cd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-61",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61 Onus",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In proceedings under this Part for review of a decision in relation\nto a request, or in relation to an application under section 48\n(a personal records application):\n(a) if an agency or a Minister applied for the review—the agency\nor Minister has the onus of establishing that the decision is\nnot justified, or that the Tribunal should give a decision\nadverse to the applicant in relation to the request or the\npersonal records application; or\n(b) if the applicant in relation to the request or the personal\nrecords application applied for the review—the agency to\nwhich, or the Minister to whom, the request or personal\nrecords application was made has the onus of establishing\nthat the decision is justified, or that the Tribunal should give\na decision adverse to the applicant.\n(2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to\ngive access to a document to which a consultation requirement\napplies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for\nthe document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the\naffected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of\nestablishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is\njustified; or\n(b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person\nwho made the relevant request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C."
    },
