    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61(2) Onus",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-61-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to\ngive access to a document to which a consultation requirement\napplies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for\nthe document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the\naffected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of\nestablishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is\njustified; or\n(b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person\nwho made the relevant request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to\ngive access to a document to which a consultation requirement\napplies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for\nthe document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the\naffected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of\nestablishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is\njustified; or\n(b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person\nwho made the relevant request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61-ss-2-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "183e8950e672196c8eebc5be7adf93c1abef8c62a4a3b06164f00258811c5d1d",
      "skos:note": "Affected third party bears the onus of establishing that a decision refusing to give access is justified or that the Tribunal should give an adverse decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-61-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61(2) Onus",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, in proceedings under this Part that relate to a decision to\ngive access to a document to which a consultation requirement\napplies under section 26A, 27 or 27A, an affected third party for\nthe document in relation to which the decision was made has, if the\naffected third party is a party to the proceeding, the onus of\nestablishing that:\n(a) a decision refusing to give access to the document is\njustified; or\n(b) the Tribunal should give a decision adverse to the person\nwho made the relevant request.\nNote:\nFor affected third party, see section 53C."
    },
