    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61A Modification of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-61a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 applies to\nproceedings under this Part as if a reference to the decision-maker\nin the following provisions of that Act were a reference to the\nagency or Minister who made the IC reviewable decision:\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nProcedure in Tribunal  Division 4\nSection 61A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) paragraph 21(2)(b) (parties and potential parties to be\nnotified of application);\n(b) section 23 (decision-maker must give Tribunal reasons and\ndocuments—general rule);\n(ba) section 24 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\nstatement if Tribunal requires—general rule);\n(bb) section 25 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\ndocuments within 28 days—general rule);\n(bc) section 26 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\ndocuments on request—general rule);\n(bd) section 27 (decision-maker must give copies of reasons and\ndocuments to other parties—general rule);\n(c) section 28 (exceptions—Tribunal may adjust requirements);\n(d) section 29 (exception—while resolving whether to restrict\npublication or disclosure of information);\n(e) paragraph 31(2)(b) (decision cannot be altered outside\nTribunal process);\n(f) section 54 (Tribunal can exercise powers of decision-maker);\n(g) subsection 56(1) (parties and their representatives to assist\nTribunal);\n(h) subsection 56(2) (parties and their representatives to assist\nTribunal);\n(i) section 60 (decision-makers may elect not to participate in\nkind of proceeding or Tribunal case event);\n(j) section 61 (decision-maker who elects not to participate may\nbe made a non-participating party to proceeding or Tribunal\ncase event);\n(k) section 65 (certain parties may seek to withdraw from being a\nparty);\n(l) subsection 79(3) (Tribunal may give directions in relation to\nprocedure for proceeding);\n(m) section 85 (Tribunal may remit decision to decision-maker\nfor reconsideration);\n(n) section 105 (Tribunal decision on review of reviewable\ndecision);",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 applies to\nproceedings under this Part as if a reference to the decision-maker\nin the following provisions of that Act were a reference to the\nagency or Minister who made the IC reviewable decision:\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nProcedure in Tribunal  Division 4\nSection 61A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) paragraph 21(2)(b) (parties and potential parties to be\nnotified of application);\n(b) section 23 (decision-maker must give Tribunal reasons and\ndocuments—general rule);\n(ba) section 24 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\nstatement if Tribunal requires—general rule);\n(bb) section 25 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\ndocuments within 28 days—general rule);\n(bc) section 26 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\ndocuments on request—general rule);\n(bd) section 27 (decision-maker must give copies of reasons and\ndocuments to other parties—general rule);\n(c) section 28 (exceptions—Tribunal may adjust requirements);\n(d) section 29 (exception—while resolving whether to restrict\npublication or disclosure of information);\n(e) paragraph 31(2)(b) (decision cannot be altered outside\nTribunal process);\n(f) section 54 (Tribunal can exercise powers of decision-maker);\n(g) subsection 56(1) (parties and their representatives to assist\nTribunal);\n(h) subsection 56(2) (parties and their representatives to assist\nTribunal);\n(i) section 60 (decision-makers may elect not to participate in\nkind of proceeding or Tribunal case event);\n(j) section 61 (decision-maker who elects not to participate may\nbe made a non-participating party to proceeding or Tribunal\ncase event);\n(k) section 65 (certain parties may seek to withdraw from being a\nparty);\n(l) subsection 79(3) (Tribunal may give directions in relation to\nprocedure for proceeding);\n(m) section 85 (Tribunal may remit decision to decision-maker\nfor reconsideration);\n(n) section 105 (Tribunal decision on review of reviewable\ndec",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61a-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "87129a516943fa54fb60f52a716e730e3899321a42614ce94db4eb9fa0900ae6",
      "skos:note": "The Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 applies to proceedings under this Part as if a reference to the decision-maker in certain provisions of that Act were a reference to the agency or Minister who made the IC reviewable decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-61a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61A Modification of the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024 applies to\nproceedings under this Part as if a reference to the decision-maker\nin the following provisions of that Act were a reference to the\nagency or Minister who made the IC reviewable decision:\n\n\nReview by the Tribunal  Part VIIA\nProcedure in Tribunal  Division 4\nSection 61A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) paragraph 21(2)(b) (parties and potential parties to be\nnotified of application);\n(b) section 23 (decision-maker must give Tribunal reasons and\ndocuments—general rule);\n(ba) section 24 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\nstatement if Tribunal requires—general rule);\n(bb) section 25 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\ndocuments within 28 days—general rule);\n(bc) section 26 (decision-maker must give Tribunal additional\ndocuments on request—general rule);\n(bd) section 27 (decision-maker must give copies of reasons and\ndocuments to other parties—general rule);\n(c) section 28 (exceptions—Tribunal may adjust requirements);\n(d) section 29 (exception—while resolving whether to restrict\npublication or disclosure of information);\n(e) paragraph 31(2)(b) (decision cannot be altered outside\nTribunal process);\n(f) section 54 (Tribunal can exercise powers of decision-maker);\n(g) subsection 56(1) (parties and their representatives to assist\nTribunal);\n(h) subsection 56(2) (parties and their representatives to assist\nTribunal);\n(i) section 60 (decision-makers may elect not to participate in\nkind of proceeding or Tribunal case event);\n(j) section 61 (decision-maker who elects not to participate may\nbe made a non-participating party to proceeding or Tribunal\ncase event);\n(k) section 65 (certain parties may seek to withdraw from being a\nparty);\n(l) subsection 79(3) (Tribunal may give directions in relation to\nprocedure for proceeding);\n(m) section 85 (Tribunal may remit decision to decision-maker\nfor reconsideration);\n(n) section 105 (Tribunal decision on review of reviewable\ndecision);"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-61a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
