    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-63",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63 Tribunal to ensure non-disclosure of certain matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-63"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.180",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 69(3) or 70(1) or (2)\nof the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024, the Tribunal must\nhave regard to:\n(a) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of\nexempt matter contained in a document to which the\nproceedings relate; and\n(b) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of\ninformation of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1).\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in the Administrative Review\nTribunal Act 2024:\n(a) the Tribunal shall not, in its decision, or reasons for a\ndecision, in a matter arising under this Act, include any\nmatter or information of a kind referred to in paragraph (1)(a)\nor (b); and\n(b) the Tribunal may receive evidence, or hear argument, in the\nabsence of the applicant or his or her representative where it\nis necessary to do so in order to prevent the disclosure to the\napplicant of matter or information of a kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a) or (b).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 69(3) or 70(1) or (2)\nof the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024, the Tribunal must\nhave regard to:\n(a) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of\nexempt matter contained in a document to which the\nproceedings relate; and\n(b) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of\ninformation of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1).\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in the Administrative Review\nTribunal Act 2024:\n(a) the Tribunal shall not, in its decision, or reasons for a\ndecision, in a matter arising under this Act, include any\nmatter or information of a kind referred to in paragraph (1)(a)\nor (b); and\n(b) the Tribunal may receive evidence, or hear argument, in the\nabsence of the applicant or his or her representative where it\nis necessary to do so in order to prevent the disclosure to the\napplicant of matter or information of a kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a) or (b).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-63-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-63-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d817756a54903cccd15ebcd6afacbc7b8ca4827355937a97e2a80d5a9357eff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 Tribunal to ensure non-disclosure of certain matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 180,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable\nto make an order or orders under subsection 69(3) or 70(1) or (2)\nof the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024, the Tribunal must\nhave regard to:\n(a) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of\nexempt matter contained in a document to which the\nproceedings relate; and\n(b) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of\ninformation of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1).\n(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in the Administrative Review\nTribunal Act 2024:\n(a) the Tribunal shall not, in its decision, or reasons for a\ndecision, in a matter arising under this Act, include any\nmatter or information of a kind referred to in paragraph (1)(a)\nor (b); and\n(b) the Tribunal may receive evidence, or hear argument, in the\nabsence of the applicant or his or her representative where it\nis necessary to do so in order to prevent the disclosure to the\napplicant of matter or information of a kind referred to in\nparagraph (1)(a) or (b)."
    },
