    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-72",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72 Information Commissioner investigations—preliminary inquiries",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-72"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "The Information Commissioner may make inquiries of the\nrespondent agency for the purpose of determining whether or not to\ninvestigate a complaint made (or purported to be made) under\nsection 70.",
      "skos:definition": "The Information Commissioner may make inquiries of the\nrespondent agency for the purpose of determining whether or not to\ninvestigate a complaint made (or purported to be made) under\nsection 70.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-72-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-72-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7861dd44b6e9ae72095186c979d1d5d8fa8a2386fe1857668e6a4e82cd2df52",
      "skos:note": "The Information Commissioner may make inquiries of the respondent agency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-72",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72 Information Commissioner investigations—preliminary inquiries",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "The Information Commissioner may make inquiries of the\nrespondent agency for the purpose of determining whether or not to\ninvestigate a complaint made (or purported to be made) under\nsection 70."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-72-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-72"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-72-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implies obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 Information Commissioner investigations—discretion not to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-73"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "investigate\nThe Information Commissioner may decide not to investigate, or\nnot to continue to investigate, a complaint about an action made\nunder section 70 if the Information Commissioner is satisfied of\nany of the following:\n(a) that the action is not taken by an agency in the performance\nof the agency’s functions or the exercise of the agency’s\npowers under this Act;\n(b) that:\n(i) the complainant has or had a right to cause the action to\nbe reviewed by the respondent agency, the Information\nCommissioner, a court or a tribunal; and\n(ii) the complainant has not exercised, or did not exercise,\nthe right; and\n(iii) it would be, or would have been, reasonable for the\ncomplainant to exercise the right;\n(c) that:\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 74\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(i) the complainant has or had a right to complain about the\naction to another body; and\n(ii) the complainant has not exercised, or did not exercise\nthe right; and\n(iii) it would be, or would have been, reasonable for the\ncomplainant to exercise the right;\n(d) that the complainant has complained to the respondent\nagency, and the respondent agency:\n(i) has dealt, or is dealing, adequately with the complaint;\nor\n(ii) has not yet had an adequate opportunity to deal with the\ncomplaint;\n(e) that the complaint is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived,\nlacking in substance or not made in good faith;\n(f) that the complainant does not have a sufficient interest in the\nsubject matter of the complaint.\nNote:\nThe Information Commissioner may make a decision under this\nsection to investigate only part of a complaint (see section 71).",
      "skos:definition": "investigate\nThe Information Commissioner may decide not to investigate, or\nnot to continue to investigate, a complaint about an action made\nunder section 70 if the Information Commissioner is satisfied of\nany of the following:\n(a) that the action is not taken by an agency in the performance\nof the agency’s functions or the exercise of the agency’s\npowers under this Act;\n(b) that:\n(i) the complainant has or had a right to cause the action to\nbe reviewed by the respondent agency, the Information\nCommissioner, a court or a tribunal; and\n(ii) the complainant has not exercised, or did not exercise,\nthe right; and\n(iii) it would be, or would have been, reasonable for the\ncomplainant to exercise the right;\n(c) that:\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 74\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(i) the complainant has or had a right to complain about the\naction to another body; and\n(ii) the complainant has not exercised, or did not exercise\nthe right; and\n(iii) it would be, or would have been, reasonable for the\ncomplainant to exercise the right;\n(d) that the complainant has complained to the respondent\nagency, and the respondent agency:\n(i) has dealt, or is dealing, adequately with the complaint;\nor\n(ii) has not yet had an adequate opportunity to deal with the\ncomplaint;\n(e) that the complaint is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived,\nlacking in substance or not made in good faith;\n(f) that the complainant does not have a sufficient interest in the\nsubject matter of the complaint.\nNote:\nThe Information Commissioner may make a decision under this\nsection to investigate only part of a complaint (see section 71).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2464448483e7a915291df14914e10e6454e1789708732a04edeeef1c49f24b5e",
      "skos:note": "Discretion not to investigate a complaint under section 70"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-73",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 Information Commissioner investigations—discretion not to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "investigate\nThe Information Commissioner may decide not to investigate, or\nnot to continue to investigate, a complaint about an action made\nunder section 70 if the Information Commissioner is satisfied of\nany of the following:\n(a) that the action is not taken by an agency in the performance\nof the agency’s functions or the exercise of the agency’s\npowers under this Act;\n(b) that:\n(i) the complainant has or had a right to cause the action to\nbe reviewed by the respondent agency, the Information\nCommissioner, a court or a tribunal; and\n(ii) the complainant has not exercised, or did not exercise,\nthe right; and\n(iii) it would be, or would have been, reasonable for the\ncomplainant to exercise the right;\n(c) that:\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 74\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(i) the complainant has or had a right to complain about the\naction to another body; and\n(ii) the complainant has not exercised, or did not exercise\nthe right; and\n(iii) it would be, or would have been, reasonable for the\ncomplainant to exercise the right;\n(d) that the complainant has complained to the respondent\nagency, and the respondent agency:\n(i) has dealt, or is dealing, adequately with the complaint;\nor\n(ii) has not yet had an adequate opportunity to deal with the\ncomplaint;\n(e) that the complaint is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived,\nlacking in substance or not made in good faith;\n(f) that the complainant does not have a sufficient interest in the\nsubject matter of the complaint.\nNote:\nThe Information Commissioner may make a decision under this\nsection to investigate only part of a complaint (see section 71)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-73-norm",
