      "cml:integrityHash": "c7d9c9a87fa3571adc752647538e9098df28005a5c013d9d9a3a8007532c0508",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with a notice requirement is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-79-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79(5) Information Commissioner investigations—obliging production",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 196,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (3); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-79-ss-5-norm",
