    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-82",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "82 Information Commissioner investigations—obliging persons to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-82"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "appear\nNotice to require person to appear\n(1) The Information Commissioner may, by written notice, require a\nperson to appear before the Information Commissioner to answer\nquestions for the purposes of an investigation.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) state that the person must comply with the notice at a\nspecified time that is not less than 14 days after the time at\nwhich the person is given the notice; and\n(c) specify the place at which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nOffence for failure to comply\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 83\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (1); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\n6 months\nimprisonment.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.",
      "skos:definition": "appear\nNotice to require person to appear\n(1) The Information Commissioner may, by written notice, require a\nperson to appear before the Information Commissioner to answer\nquestions for the purposes of an investigation.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) state that the person must comply with the notice at a\nspecified time that is not less than 14 days after the time at\nwhich the person is given the notice; and\n(c) specify the place at which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nOffence for failure to comply\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 83\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (1); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\n6 months\nimprisonment.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-82-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-82-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-82-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a30c70ad406980226ecca3beadfb8dfa676bbf52a9a4e5d443c012704ee0db87"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-82",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "82 Information Commissioner investigations—obliging persons to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "appear\nNotice to require person to appear\n(1) The Information Commissioner may, by written notice, require a\nperson to appear before the Information Commissioner to answer\nquestions for the purposes of an investigation.\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) be in writing; and\n(b) state that the person must comply with the notice at a\nspecified time that is not less than 14 days after the time at\nwhich the person is given the notice; and\n(c) specify the place at which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nOffence for failure to comply\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 83\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice\nunder subsection (1); and\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n(c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty for a contravention of this subsection:\n6 months\nimprisonment.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility."
    },
