    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-85",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85 Information Commissioner investigations—protection from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-85"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.200",
      "values:originalText": "liability\n(1) This section applies if a person does any of the following in good\nfaith for the purposes of an investigation:\n(a) gives information;\n(b) produces a document;\n(c) answers a question.\n(2) If this section applies, then:\n(a) civil proceedings do not lie against a person because the\nperson does any of the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs (1)(a) to (c); and\n(b) the person is not liable for a penalty under a provision of any\nlaw because the person does any of those matters.\n(3) This section applies whether or not the person is required to do a\nthing mentioned in subsection (1) in accordance with this Division.\nSubdivision E—Outcome of investigation",
      "skos:definition": "liability\n(1) This section applies if a person does any of the following in good\nfaith for the purposes of an investigation:\n(a) gives information;\n(b) produces a document;\n(c) answers a question.\n(2) If this section applies, then:\n(a) civil proceedings do not lie against a person because the\nperson does any of the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs (1)(a) to (c); and\n(b) the person is not liable for a penalty under a provision of any\nlaw because the person does any of those matters.\n(3) This section applies whether or not the person is required to do a\nthing mentioned in subsection (1) in accordance with this Division.\nSubdivision E—Outcome of investigation",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-85-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-85-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-85-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5fd94b8c335618802e86694c5bfc293a5bc68c6200fe46c550cf2b24ac595f3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-85",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85 Information Commissioner investigations—protection from",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 200,
      "values:originalText": "liability\n(1) This section applies if a person does any of the following in good\nfaith for the purposes of an investigation:\n(a) gives information;\n(b) produces a document;\n(c) answers a question.\n(2) If this section applies, then:\n(a) civil proceedings do not lie against a person because the\nperson does any of the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs (1)(a) to (c); and\n(b) the person is not liable for a penalty under a provision of any\nlaw because the person does any of those matters.\n(3) This section applies whether or not the person is required to do a\nthing mentioned in subsection (1) in accordance with this Division.\nSubdivision E—Outcome of investigation"
    },
