      "cml:premiseText": "The investigation recommendations, in relation to the investigation...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The recommendations are made during the investigation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "89 Information Commissioner investigations—failure to implement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-89"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.202",
      "values:originalText": "investigation recommendation\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the Information Commissioner completes an investigation;\nand\n(b) the Information Commissioner gives an agency a notice\nunder section 86; and\n(c) the Information Commissioner is not satisfied that the agency\nhas taken action that is adequate and appropriate in the\ncircumstances to implement the investigation\nrecommendations for the investigation.\nGiving implementation notices\n(2) The Information Commissioner may, by notice in writing (an\nimplementation notice), require the respondent agency to:\n(a) give to the Information Commissioner particulars of any\naction that the agency proposes to take to implement the\ninvestigation recommendations for the investigation; and\n(b) give the particulars within the time specified in the notice.\n(3) The respondent agency must comply with the implementation\nnotice.\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 89A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "skos:definition": "investigation recommendation\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the Information Commissioner completes an investigation;\nand\n(b) the Information Commissioner gives an agency a notice\nunder section 86; and\n(c) the Information Commissioner is not satisfied that the agency\nhas taken action that is adequate and appropriate in the\ncircumstances to implement the investigation\nrecommendations for the investigation.\nGiving implementation notices\n(2) The Information Commissioner may, by notice in writing (an\nimplementation notice), require the respondent agency to:\n(a) give to the Information Commissioner particulars of any\naction that the agency proposes to take to implement the\ninvestigation recommendations for the investigation; and\n(b) give the particulars within the time specified in the notice.\n(3) The respondent agency must comply with the implementation\nnotice.\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 89A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c08d28b85e8466daaba336478f3ba3e51d1aab8ff0712623051c902b4ed518fe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-89",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "89 Information Commissioner investigations—failure to implement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "investigation recommendation\nScope\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) the Information Commissioner completes an investigation;\nand\n(b) the Information Commissioner gives an agency a notice\nunder section 86; and\n(c) the Information Commissioner is not satisfied that the agency\nhas taken action that is adequate and appropriate in the\ncircumstances to implement the investigation\nrecommendations for the investigation.\nGiving implementation notices\n(2) The Information Commissioner may, by notice in writing (an\nimplementation notice), require the respondent agency to:\n(a) give to the Information Commissioner particulars of any\naction that the agency proposes to take to implement the\ninvestigation recommendations for the investigation; and\n(b) give the particulars within the time specified in the notice.\n(3) The respondent agency must comply with the implementation\nnotice.\n\n\nInvestigations and complaints  Part VIIB\nInformation Commissioner investigations  Division 2\nSection 89A\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
    {
