    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-89j-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "89J(2) Complaints to Ombudsman—limitation on amending records in",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 208,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Ombudsman must not, in a report under section 15 of the\nOmbudsman Act 1976, recommend that an amendment be made to\na record if he or she is satisfied of either of the following:\n(a) the record is a record of a decision, under an enactment or a\nNorfolk Island law, by a court, tribunal, authority or person;\n(b) the decision whether to amend the record involves\ndetermination of a question that the person seeking\namendment of the record is, or has been, entitled to have\ndetermined by the agency (on internal review), the\nInformation Commissioner, a court or tribunal.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part VIII\nVexatious applicants  Division 1\nSection 89K\nFreedom of Information Act 1982\nCompilation date: 01/01/2026"
    },
