      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12b311ae6c0276c0129d0d5fda3981319ce2c3cace9ece6efc482810ed18eb7a",
      "skos:note": "Minister or officer not committing a criminal offence due to good faith actions under Part II or section 11C."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-92-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92(1) Protection against criminal liability",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 215,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Minister, or an officer of an agency, does not commit a criminal\noffence only because the Minister or officer:\n(a) publishes a document in good faith, in the belief that the\npublication is required or permitted under Part II\n(information publication scheme) or section 11C (publication\nof information in accessed documents); or\n(b) gives access to a document in good faith, in the belief that the\naccess is required or permitted to be given in response to a\nrequest; or\n(c) publishes, or gives access to, a document in good faith, in the\nbelief that the publication or access is required or permitted\notherwise than under this Act (whether or not under an\nexpress legislative power)."
    },
