          "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-92-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f619a4ca09c44e6e91845d3001d47ecde0e5fa08e2c958933a906fd53dc83352",
      "skos:note": "Protection against criminal liability for showing documents to State or organisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/freedom-of-information-act-1982#sch-4-sec-92-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92(2) Protection against criminal liability",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 215,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person does not commit a criminal offence only because the\nperson shows a document, or is concerned in the showing of a\ndocument, to another person or organisation for any of the\nfollowing purposes:\n(a) consultation with a State under subsection 26A(2);\n(b) enabling the other person or the organisation to make a\nsubmission under subsection 27(4);\n(c) enabling the other person to make a submission under\nsubsection 27A(3)."
    },
